window.DOCS["6ae39ed27b12c517cf05e7cd"]={"id":"6ae39ed27b12c517cf05e7cd","summary":{"title_zh":"第二工作小組報告草案","what":"這份文件是第二工作小組的報告草案（CBD/COP/17/WG.II/L.1 與 CBD/CP/MOP/12/WG.II/L.1），記錄其在葉里溫會議期間，對生物多樣性公約第十七次締約方大會及卡塔赫納生物安全議定書第十二次締約方會議各項議程之審議過程，並將提交各會議通過。","points":["第16項（合成生物學）：成立聯絡小組，處理決議草案中與主題行動計畫（能力建構、技術轉移與知識分享）相關的括號文字（第4段）。","第17(a)項（策略性審查）與第17(d)項（潛在進一步工作）：成立聯絡小組處理括號文字並擬定乾淨文本（第7、29段）；第17(e)項（平台工作計畫）另成立聯絡小組，以達成共識並定稿（第32段）。","第17(b)項（森林生物多樣性工作計畫）：主席成立主席之友小組，處理草案剩餘問題（包括附件）（第17段）。","第17(c)項（保護區工作計畫）：成立聯絡小組處理括號文字，包括工作計畫之標題、範圍與生態系連結性（第26段）。","第18(a)項（生物多樣性與氣候變遷）：成立聯絡小組處理未決事項（第40段）；第18(b)項（永續野生生物管理）與第18(c)項（海洋與海岸及島嶼生物多樣性）亦分別成立聯絡小組處理括號文字（第44、48段）。","第18(d)項（生物多樣性與農業）與第18(e)項（外來入侵種）：草案經口頭修正後核可，分別送交全體會議（第18(d)項為草案編號 L.xx，第18(e)項為 L.5）（第63、72段）。","第18(f)項（生物多樣性與健康）：成立聯絡小組處理括號文字，修改限於進度報告（第81段）。","卡塔赫納議定書事項：第5、7、8、9、10、13、14、15、16、17項之決議草案已核可，分別為 CBD/CP/MOP/12/L.2、L.6、L.10、L.9、L.5、L.11、L.7、L.4、L.8、L.3；第11項僅備悉（第92、100、109、126、134、146、155、164、173、183、140段）。"],"open":["全文多處段落標註「to be completed」（第2、5、8、24、27、30、33、42、46、52、73、85段）尚未補齊，報告內容未定稿。","第16項（合成生物學）：括號文字之決議內容（第4段）。","第17(a)、(d)、(e)項：括號文字與乾淨文本尚未完成（第7、29、32段）。","第17(b)項：森林工作計畫附件之剩餘文字（第17段）。","第17(c)項：保護區工作計畫之標題、範圍與生態系連結性（第26段）。","第18(a)項：生物多樣性與氣候變遷決議草案之未決事項（第40段）。","第18(b)項：永續野生生物管理決議草案之括號文字（第44段）。","第18(c)項：海洋與海岸及島嶼生物多樣性之括號文字，以及主席修訂草案之後續審議（第48、49段）。","第18(f)項：生物多樣性與健康相關之括號文字（第81段）。"]},"summaryReviewed":true,"pages":[{"p":"p001","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ae39ed27b12c517cf05e7cd/p001.md","en":[{"t":"CBD/COP/17/WG.II/L.1-CBD/CP/MOP/12/WG.II/L.1"},{"t":"Distr.: Limited 28 October 2026 Original: English"},{"t":"Conference of the Parties to the Convention                   Conference of the Parties to the Convention\non Biological Diversity                                       on Biological Diversity serving as the meeting\nSeventeenth meeting                                           of the Parties to the Cartagena Protocol on\nYerevan, 19–30 October 2026                                   Biosafety\nAgenda item 22                                                Twelfth meeting\nAdoption of the report                                        Yerevan, 19–30 October 2026","tb":1},{"t":"Agenda item 19"},{"t":"Adoption of the report"},{"t":"Draft report of Working Group II"},{"t":"Introduction"},{"t":"1.    Working Group II, chaired by Hesiquio Benítez Díaz, met to consider items 16, 17 (a) to (e) and 18 (a) to (f) of the agenda for the seventeenth meeting of the Conference of the Parties to the Convention on Biological Diversity (see sect. I) and items 5, 7 to 11 and 13 to 17 of the agenda for the twelfth meeting of the Parties to the Cartagena Protocol on Biosafety (see sect. II)."},{"t":"2.     [to be completed]"},{"t":"I.     Seventeenth meeting of the Conference of the Parties"},{"t":"to the Convention on Biological Diversity"},{"t":"Item 16"},{"t":"Synthetic biology"},{"t":"3.     Working Group II began its consideration of agenda item 16 at its 1st session, on 19 October. It had before it a draft decision.1"},{"t":"4.    Working Group II agreed to establish a contact group, co-chaired by Onyeka Nwosu (Nigeria) and Valeria Giovannelli (Italy), with the mandate to resolve the bracketed text in the draft decision, which related to the thematic action plan to support capacity-building and development, access to and transfer of technology and knowledge-sharing in the context of synthetic biology for the implementation of the Convention and the Kunming-Montreal Global Biodiversity Framework and how to address the most recent technological developments in synthetic biology."},{"t":"5.     [to be completed]"},{"t":"1 CBD/COP/17/2, item 16."}],"blocks":[{"md":"CBD/COP/17/WG.II/L.1-CBD/CP/MOP/12/WG.II/L.1\n發行：限閱\n2026年10月28日\n原文：英文","html":"<p>CBD/COP/17/WG.II/L.1-CBD/CP/MOP/12/WG.II/L.1<br />\n發行：限閱<br />\n2026年10月28日<br />\n原文：英文</p>","en":[0,1]},{"md":"生物多樣性公約締約方大會\n第十七次會議\n葉里溫，2026年10月19–30日\n議程項目 22\n報告之採納","html":"<p>生物多樣性公約締約方大會<br />\n第十七次會議<br />\n葉里溫，2026年10月19–30日<br />\n議程項目 22<br />\n報告之採納</p>","en":[2]},{"md":"以卡塔赫納生物安全議定書締約方會議形式召開之\n生物多樣性公約締約方大會\n第十二次會議\n葉里溫，2026年10月19–30日\n議程項目 19\n報告之採納","html":"<p>以卡塔赫納生物安全議定書締約方會議形式召開之<br />\n生物多樣性公約締約方大會<br />\n第十二次會議<br />\n葉里溫，2026年10月19–30日<br />\n議程項目 19<br />\n報告之採納</p>","en":[2]},{"md":"第二工作小組報告草案\n引言\n1.\n由 Hesiquio Benítez Díaz 主席之第二工作小組已召開會議，以審議生物多樣性公約締約方大會第十七次會議議程之項目 16、17 (a) 至 (e) 及 18 (a) 至 (f)（見第一節），以及卡塔赫納生物安全議定書第十二次締約方會議議程之項目 5、7 至 11 及 13 至 17（見第二節）。\n2.\n[待完成]","html":"<p>第二工作小組報告草案<br />\n引言<br />\n1.<br />\n由 Hesiquio Benítez Díaz 主席之第二工作小組已召開會議，以審議生物多樣性公約締約方大會第十七次會議議程之項目 16、17 (a) 至 (e) 及 18 (a) 至 (f)（見第一節），以及卡塔赫納生物安全議定書第十二次締約方會議議程之項目 5、7 至 11 及 13 至 17（見第二節）。<br />\n2.<br />\n[待完成]</p>","en":[3,4,5,6,7]},{"md":"I.","html":"<p>I.</p>","en":[8]},{"md":"生物多樣性公約締約方大會第十七次會議","html":"<p>生物多樣性公約締約方大會第十七次會議</p>","pre":"第二節）。\n2.\n[待完成]\n\nI.\n\n","en":[9]},{"md":"項目 16\n合成生物學\n3.\n第二工作小組於10月19日的第一個會議開始審議議程項目 16。其面前有一份決議草案。¹\n4.\n第二工作小組同意成立一個聯絡小組，由 Onyeka Nwosu (奈及利亞) 與 Valeria Giovannelli (義大利) 共同主持，其任務為解決決議草案中方括號內的文字，該文字涉及：為落實本公約與《昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要》，在合成生物學範疇內，支持能力建構與發展、技術取得與轉讓以及知識分享之主題行動計畫，以及如何應對合成生物學最新技術發展之議題。\n5.","html":"<p>項目 16<br />\n合成生物學<br />\n3.<br />\n第二工作小組於10月19日的第一個會議開始審議議程項目 16。其面前有一份決議草案。¹<br />\n4.<br />\n第二工作小組同意成立一個聯絡小組，由 Onyeka Nwosu (奈及利亞) 與 Valeria Giovannelli (義大利) 共同主持，其任務為解決決議草案中方括號內的文字，該文字涉及：為落實本公約與《昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要》，在合成生物學範疇內，支持能力建構與發展、技術取得與轉讓以及知識分享之主題行動計畫，以及如何應對合成生物學最新技術發展之議題。<br />\n5.</p>","en":[10,11,12,13,14]},{"md":"[待完成]","html":"<p>[待完成]</p>","pre":"合成生物學最新技術發展之議題。\n5.\n\n","en":[15]},{"md":"¹ CBD/COP/17/2, 項目 16。","html":"<p>¹ CBD/COP/17/2, 項目 16。</p>","en":[16]}]},{"p":"p002","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ae39ed27b12c517cf05e7cd/p002.md","en":[{"t":"CBD/COP/17/WG.II/L.1-CBD/CP/MOP/12/WG.II/L.1"},{"t":"Item 17"},{"t":"Scientific and technical needs to support the implementation of the Kunming-Montreal Global Biodiversity Framework and matters related to the work programme of the Intergovernmental Science-Policy Platform on Biodiversity and Ecosystem Services"},{"t":"(a) Strategic review and analysis of the programmes of work under the Convention on Biological Diversity in the context of the Framework"},{"t":"6.     Working Group II began its consideration of agenda item 17 (a) at its 1st session. It had before it a draft decision2 and a note by the Secretariat on the approach and methodology for the strategic review and analysis of the programmes of work under the Convention in the context of the Kunming- Montreal Global Biodiversity Framework.3"},{"t":"7.    Working Group II agreed to establish a contact group, co-chaired by Nneka Nicholas (Antigua and Barbuda) and Senka Barudanović (Bosnia and Herzegovina), with the mandate to resolve the bracketed text and prepare a clean text of the draft decision."},{"t":"8.      [to be completed]"},{"t":"(b) Strategic review of and updates to the expanded programme of work on forest biodiversity"},{"t":"9.      Working Group II began its consideration of agenda item 17 (b) at its 1st session. It had before it a draft decision.4"},{"t":"10. The Chair said that he would conduct informal consultations as needed and prepare a revised version of the draft decision in consultation with the Secretariat."},{"t":"11. At its 3rd session, on 20 October, the Working Group began its consideration of a draft decision submitted by the Chair."},{"t":"12. Statements were made by representatives of the following Parties: Argentina, Bangladesh, Brazil, Canada, European Union and its member States, India, Iran (Islamic Republic of), Japan, Mexico, Namibia, Norway, Panama, Papua New Guinea (on behalf of the Pacific small island developing States), Russian Federation, Saudi Arabia, South Africa, Suriname, Switzerland, Uganda and Zimbabwe."},{"t":"13. The Chair invited representatives of Argentina, Brazil, the European Union, Namibia, the Russian Federation and Suriname to hold informal consultations, with a view to reaching consensus on the wording of the annex to the draft decision."},{"t":"14. At its 4th session, on 21 October, Working Group II resumed its consideration of the draft decision."},{"t":"15. The representative of the European Union reported that the informal consultations on the wording of the annex to the draft decision had not taken place, owing to a lack of time."},{"t":"16. Statements were made by representatives of the following Parties: Argentina, Brazil, Chile, China, Colombia, Costa Rica, European Union and its member States, India, Kyrgyzstan, Namibia, Nigeria, Norway, Panama, Russian Federation, South Africa, Switzerland, United Kingdom of Great Britain and Northern Ireland and Uruguay."},{"t":"17. The Chair established a group of friends of the Chair with the mandate to resolve the remaining issues in the draft decision, including in its annex."},{"t":"2Ibid., sub-item 17 (a)."},{"t":"3 CBD/COP/17/10."},{"t":"4 CBD/COP/17/2, sub-item 17 (b)."},{"t":"2/15"}],"blocks":[{"md":"CBD/COP/17/WG.II/L.1-CBD/CP/MOP/12/WG.II/L.1","html":"<p>CBD/COP/17/WG.II/L.1-CBD/CP/MOP/12/WG.II/L.1</p>","en":[0,1]},{"md":"項目 17\n支持實施昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要之科學與技術需求，以及與生物多樣性及生態系政府間科學－政策平台工作計畫相關事項\n(a) 在綱要脈絡下，對《生物多樣性公約》架構下工作計畫進行策略性審查與分析\n6.\n第二工作小組於其第 1 次會議開始審議議程項目 17 (a)。其面前有一份決議草案$^2$以及秘書處關於在昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要脈絡下，對《公約》架構下工作計畫進行策略性審查與分析之方法與方法論的說明文件$^3$。\n7.\n第二工作小組同意成立一個聯絡小組，由 Nneka Nicholas（安地卡及巴布達）與 Senka Barudanović（波士尼亞與赫塞哥維納）共同主持，其任務為解決方括號文字並準備決議草案的整理稿。\n8.","html":"<p>項目 17<br />\n支持實施昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要之科學與技術需求，以及與生物多樣性及生態系政府間科學－政策平台工作計畫相關事項<br />\n(a) 在綱要脈絡下，對《生物多樣性公約》架構下工作計畫進行策略性審查與分析<br />\n6.<br />\n第二工作小組於其第 1 次會議開始審議議程項目 17 (a)。其面前有一份決議草案<sup>2</sup>以及秘書處關於在昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要脈絡下，對《公約》架構下工作計畫進行策略性審查與分析之方法與方法論的說明文件<sup>3</sup>。<br />\n7.<br />\n第二工作小組同意成立一個聯絡小組，由 Nneka Nicholas（安地卡及巴布達）與 Senka Barudanović（波士尼亞與赫塞哥維納）共同主持，其任務為解決方括號文字並準備決議草案的整理稿。<br />\n8.</p>","en":[2,3,4,5,6]},{"md":"[待完成]","html":"<p>[待完成]</p>","en":[7,8,9,10]},{"md":"(b) 對森林生物多樣性擴大工作計畫進行策略性審查與更新\n9.\n第二工作小組於其第 1 次會議開始審議議程項目 17 (b)。其面前有一份決議草案$^4$。\n10. 主席表示，他將視需要進行非正式諮商，並與秘書處諮商後準備決議草案的修訂版本。\n11. 在其第 3 次會議（10 月 20 日）期間，工作小組開始審議由主席提交的決議草案。\n12. 以下締約方代表發表了聲明：阿根廷、孟加拉、巴西、加拿大、歐盟及其成員國、印度、伊朗（伊斯蘭共和國）、日本、墨西哥、納米比亞、挪威、巴拿馬、巴布亞紐幾內亞（代表太平洋小島嶼開發中國家）、俄羅斯聯邦、沙烏地阿拉伯、南非、蘇利南、瑞士、烏干達及辛巴威。\n13. 主席邀請阿根廷、巴西、歐盟、納米比亞、俄羅斯聯邦及蘇利南的代表進行非正式諮商，旨在就決議草案附件的措辭達成共識。\n14. 在其第 4 次會議（10 月 21 日）期間，第二工作小組恢復審議該決議草案。\n15. 歐盟代表報告，由於時間不足，決議草案附件措辭的非正式諮商尚未舉行。\n16. 以下締約方代表發表了聲明：阿根廷、巴西、智利、中國、哥倫比亞、哥斯大黎加、歐盟及其成員國、印度、吉爾吉斯、納米比亞、奈及利亞、挪威、巴拿馬、俄羅斯聯邦、南非、瑞士、英國（大不列顛及北愛爾蘭）及烏拉圭。\n17. 主席成立了一個主席之友小組，其任務為解決決議草案（包括其附件）中剩餘的問題。","html":"<p>(b) 對森林生物多樣性擴大工作計畫進行策略性審查與更新<br />\n9.<br />\n第二工作小組於其第 1 次會議開始審議議程項目 17 (b)。其面前有一份決議草案<sup>4</sup>。<br />\n10. 主席表示，他將視需要進行非正式諮商，並與秘書處諮商後準備決議草案的修訂版本。<br />\n11. 在其第 3 次會議（10 月 20 日）期間，工作小組開始審議由主席提交的決議草案。<br />\n12. 以下締約方代表發表了聲明：阿根廷、孟加拉、巴西、加拿大、歐盟及其成員國、印度、伊朗（伊斯蘭共和國）、日本、墨西哥、納米比亞、挪威、巴拿馬、巴布亞紐幾內亞（代表太平洋小島嶼開發中國家）、俄羅斯聯邦、沙烏地阿拉伯、南非、蘇利南、瑞士、烏干達及辛巴威。<br />\n13. 主席邀請阿根廷、巴西、歐盟、納米比亞、俄羅斯聯邦及蘇利南的代表進行非正式諮商，旨在就決議草案附件的措辭達成共識。<br />\n14. 在其第 4 次會議（10 月 21 日）期間，第二工作小組恢復審議該決議草案。<br />\n15. 歐盟代表報告，由於時間不足，決議草案附件措辭的非正式諮商尚未舉行。<br />\n16. 以下締約方代表發表了聲明：阿根廷、巴西、智利、中國、哥倫比亞、哥斯大黎加、歐盟及其成員國、印度、吉爾吉斯、納米比亞、奈及利亞、挪威、巴拿馬、俄羅斯聯邦、南非、瑞士、英國（大不列顛及北愛爾蘭）及烏拉圭。<br />\n17. 主席成立了一個主席之友小組，其任務為解決決議草案（包括其附件）中剩餘的問題。</p>","en":[11,12,13,14,15]},{"md":"$^2$ 同前引，子項目 17 (a)。\n$^3$ CBD/COP/17/10。\n$^4$ CBD/COP/17/2，子項目 17 (b)。","html":"<p><sup>2</sup> 同前引，子項目 17 (a)。<br />\n<sup>3</sup> CBD/COP/17/10。<br />\n<sup>4</sup> CBD/COP/17/2，子項目 17 (b)。</p>","en":[16,17,18,19]},{"md":"2/15","html":"<p>2/15</p>","en":[20]}]},{"p":"p003","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ae39ed27b12c517cf05e7cd/p003.md","en":[{"t":"CBD/COP/17/WG.II/L.1-CBD/CP/MOP/12/WG.II/L.1"},{"t":"18. At its 8th session, on 27 October, following a report by a representative of the Secretariat on the outcome of the work of the group of friends of the Chair, Working Group II resumed its consideration of the draft decision."},{"t":"19. Statements were made by representatives of the following Parties: Argentina, Australia, Brazil, Canada, China, European Union and its member States, Guatemala, Norway, Panama, Papua New Guinea (on behalf of the Pacific small island developing States), Russian Federation, Saudi Arabia, Tuvalu, Uruguay and Zimbabwe."},{"t":"20. At its 9th session, on 27 October, Working Group II resumed its consideration of the draft decision."},{"t":"21. Statements were made by representatives of the following Parties: Brazil, Canada, Chile, Colombia, European Union and its member States, India, Iran (Islamic Republic of), Mexico, Namibia, Norway, Panama, Russian Federation, Tuvalu and Uganda."},{"t":"22. At its 10th session, on 28 October, Working Group II resumed its consideration of the draft decision."},{"t":"23. Statements were made by representatives of the following Parties: Bangladesh, Brazil, European Union and its member States, Norway, Panama, Russian Federation, Tuvalu, Uruguay and Zimbabwe."},{"t":"24.     [to be completed]"},{"t":"(c)     Strategic review of and updates to the programme of work on protected areas"},{"t":"25. Working Group II began its consideration of agenda item 17 (c) at its 1st session. It had before it a draft decision.5"},{"t":"26. Working Group II agreed to establish a contact group, co-chaired by Ruliyana Susanti (Indonesia) and Julie Hammer-Monart (France), with the mandate to resolve the bracketed text in the draft decision, including in connection with the title and scope of the programme of work and with ecological connectivity."},{"t":"27.     [to be completed]"},{"t":"(d)     Areas of potential further work in the context of the Framework"},{"t":"28. Working Group II began its consideration of agenda item 17 (d) at its 1st session. It had before it a draft decision. 6 An information document containing a compilation of information on the activities of multilateral agreements, organizations and processes on the interaction of chemicals and waste, including plastic waste, with biodiversity and ecosystem services7 had also been issued in relation to sub-item 17 (d)."},{"t":"29. Working Group II agreed that the contact group established under agenda item 17 (a) would also address the draft decision under sub-item 17 (d), with the mandate to resolve the bracketed text in the draft decision, basing its work on text prepared by the Chair with the assistance of the Secretariat."},{"t":"30.     [to be completed]"},{"t":"5 Ibid., sub-item 17 (c)."},{"t":"6 Ibid., sub-item 17 (d)."},{"t":"7 CBD/COP/17/INF/23."},{"t":"3/15"}],"blocks":[{"md":"CBD/COP/17/WG.II/L.1-CBD/CP/MOP/12/WG.II/L.1","html":"<p>CBD/COP/17/WG.II/L.1-CBD/CP/MOP/12/WG.II/L.1</p>","en":[0,1]},{"md":"18. 在第 8 次會議中，於 10 月 27 日，在秘書處代表就主席之友小組工作成果進行報告後，第二工作小組恢復對決議草案的審議。\n19. 以下締約方代表發表了聲明：阿根廷、澳洲、巴西、加拿大、中國、歐盟及其成員國、瓜地馬拉、挪威、巴拿馬、巴布亞紐幾內亞（代表太平洋小島嶼開發中國家）、俄羅斯聯邦、沙烏地阿拉伯、吐瓦魯、烏拉圭及辛巴威。\n20. 在第 9 次會議中，於 10 月 27 日，第二工作小組恢復對決議草案的審議。\n21. 以下締約方代表發表了聲明：巴西、加拿大、智利、哥倫比亞、歐盟及其成員國、印度、伊朗（伊斯蘭共和國）、墨西哥、納米比亞、挪威、巴拿馬、俄羅斯聯邦、吐瓦魯及烏干達。\n22. 在第 10 次會議中，於 10 月 28 日，第二工作小組恢復對決議草案的審議。\n23. 以下締約方代表發表了聲明：孟加拉、巴西、歐盟及其成員國、挪威、巴拿馬、俄羅斯聯邦、吐瓦魯、烏拉圭及辛巴威。\n24.","html":"<p>18. 在第 8 次會議中，於 10 月 27 日，在秘書處代表就主席之友小組工作成果進行報告後，第二工作小組恢復對決議草案的審議。<br />\n19. 以下締約方代表發表了聲明：阿根廷、澳洲、巴西、加拿大、中國、歐盟及其成員國、瓜地馬拉、挪威、巴拿馬、巴布亞紐幾內亞（代表太平洋小島嶼開發中國家）、俄羅斯聯邦、沙烏地阿拉伯、吐瓦魯、烏拉圭及辛巴威。<br />\n20. 在第 9 次會議中，於 10 月 27 日，第二工作小組恢復對決議草案的審議。<br />\n21. 以下締約方代表發表了聲明：巴西、加拿大、智利、哥倫比亞、歐盟及其成員國、印度、伊朗（伊斯蘭共和國）、墨西哥、納米比亞、挪威、巴拿馬、俄羅斯聯邦、吐瓦魯及烏干達。<br />\n22. 在第 10 次會議中，於 10 月 28 日，第二工作小組恢復對決議草案的審議。<br />\n23. 以下締約方代表發表了聲明：孟加拉、巴西、歐盟及其成員國、挪威、巴拿馬、俄羅斯聯邦、吐瓦魯、烏拉圭及辛巴威。<br />\n24.</p>","en":[2,3,4,5,6]},{"md":"(c)","html":"<p>(c)</p>","pre":"邦、吐瓦魯、烏拉圭及辛巴威。\n24.\n\n","en":[7]},{"md":"[待完成]","html":"<p>[待完成]</p>","pre":"、烏拉圭及辛巴威。\n24.\n\n(c)\n\n","en":[7]},{"md":"針對保護區工作計畫進行策略性審查與更新\n25. 第二工作小組於第 1 次會議開始審議議程項目 17 (c)。其面前有一份決議草案。⁵\n26. 第二工作小組同意成立一個聯絡小組，由 Ruliyana Susanti（印尼）與 Julie Hammer-Monart（法國）共同主持，其任務是解決決議草案中的方括號文字，包括與工作計畫之標題與範圍以及生態連結相關之內容。\n27.","html":"<p>針對保護區工作計畫進行策略性審查與更新<br />\n25. 第二工作小組於第 1 次會議開始審議議程項目 17 (c)。其面前有一份決議草案。⁵<br />\n26. 第二工作小組同意成立一個聯絡小組，由 Ruliyana Susanti（印尼）與 Julie Hammer-Monart（法國）共同主持，其任務是解決決議草案中的方括號文字，包括與工作計畫之標題與範圍以及生態連結相關之內容。<br />\n27.</p>","en":[8,9,10]},{"md":"(d)","html":"<p>(d)</p>","pre":"範圍以及生態連結相關之內容。\n27.\n\n","en":[11]},{"md":"[待完成]","html":"<p>[待完成]</p>","pre":"態連結相關之內容。\n27.\n\n(d)\n\n","en":[11]},{"md":"在綱要脈絡下潛在進一步工作之領域\n28. 第二工作小組於第 1 次會議開始審議議程項目 17 (d)。其面前有一份決議草案。⁶ 此外，針對子項目 17 (d)，亦已發布一份資訊文件，其中彙編了關於化學品與廢棄物（包括塑膠廢棄物）與生物多樣性及生態系服務交互作用之多邊協議、組織與程序活動的資訊。⁷\n29. 第二工作小組同意，根據議程項目 17 (a) 所成立的聯絡小組亦將處理子項目 17 (d) 下的決議草案，其任務是解決決議草案中的方括號文字，並在其工作基礎上使用由主席在秘書處協助下所準備之文字。\n30.","html":"<p>在綱要脈絡下潛在進一步工作之領域<br />\n28. 第二工作小組於第 1 次會議開始審議議程項目 17 (d)。其面前有一份決議草案。⁶ 此外，針對子項目 17 (d)，亦已發布一份資訊文件，其中彙編了關於化學品與廢棄物（包括塑膠廢棄物）與生物多樣性及生態系服務交互作用之多邊協議、組織與程序活動的資訊。⁷<br />\n29. 第二工作小組同意，根據議程項目 17 (a) 所成立的聯絡小組亦將處理子項目 17 (d) 下的決議草案，其任務是解決決議草案中的方括號文字，並在其工作基礎上使用由主席在秘書處協助下所準備之文字。<br />\n30.</p>","en":[12,13,14]},{"md":"[待完成]","html":"<p>[待完成]</p>","pre":"在秘書處協助下所準備之文字。\n30.\n\n","en":[15]},{"md":"⁵ 同前，子項目 17 (c)。\n⁶ 同前，子項目 17 (d)。\n⁷ CBD/COP/17/INF/23。","html":"<p>⁵ 同前，子項目 17 (c)。<br />\n⁶ 同前，子項目 17 (d)。<br />\n⁷ CBD/COP/17/INF/23。</p>","en":[16,17,18,19]}]},{"p":"p004","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ae39ed27b12c517cf05e7cd/p004.md","en":[{"t":"CBD/COP/17/WG.II/L.1-CBD/CP/MOP/12/WG.II/L.1"},{"t":"(e)     Matters related to the work programme of the Platform"},{"t":"31. Working Group II began its consideration of agenda item 17 (e) at its 1st session. It had before it a draft decision.8"},{"t":"32. Working Group II agreed to establish a contact group, co-chaired by Dickson Chitupa (Zimbabwe) and Elif Skinner (United Kingdom), with the mandate to reach consensus on the bracketed text and finalize the text of the draft decision."},{"t":"33.     [to be completed]"},{"t":"Item 18"},{"t":"Other scientific and technical issues related to the implementation of the Kunming- Montreal Global Biodiversity Framework"},{"t":"(a)     Biodiversity and climate change"},{"t":"34. Working Group II began its consideration of agenda item 18 (a) at its 1st session. It had before it a draft decision9 and a progress report by the Secretariat on activities on biodiversity and climate change. 10 Two information documents had also been issued in relation to sub-item 18 (a): an expanded supplement to the voluntary guidelines for the design and effective implementation of ecosystem-based approaches to climate change adaptation and disaster risk reduction 11 and a mapping study on actions, gaps and overlaps for enhancing cooperation and policy coherence and synergies across the Rio conventions.12"},{"t":"35. As the modalities for the early submission of statements13 had been implemented for agenda item 18 (a), with statements submitted on an informal and voluntary basis pursuant to notification No. 2026-072 of the Secretariat, the Chair asked the Parties and observers listed in annex II to document CBD/COP/17/INF/24 and present at the session whether they objected to their statements being considered as statements officially submitted for the present sub-item. No objections were raised."},{"t":"36. Working Group II therefore agreed that the statements of the following Parties be considered as statements officially submitted under agenda item 18 (a): Australia, Bangladesh, Brazil, Canada, China, Côte d’Ivoire, Cuba, European Union and its member States, Fiji (on behalf of the Pacific small island developing States), Guatemala, Iceland, Japan, Jordan, Madagascar, Maldives, Morocco, Nepal, New Zealand, Norway, Republic of Korea, Senegal, Suriname, Switzerland and United Kingdom."},{"t":"37. Working Group II also agreed that statements of the following observers be considered as statements officially submitted under agenda item 18 (a): Alliance of Bioversity International and the International Center for Tropical Agriculture, CGIAR, Division for Ocean Affairs and the Law of the Sea of the United Nations, CBD Women’s Caucus, Exploring Womanhood Foundation, Fungi Foundation, Global Youth Biodiversity Network, Greenpeace International, Inter-American Institute for Global Change Research, International Chamber of Commerce, International Indigenous Forum on Biodiversity, International Union for Conservation of Nature, Office of the United Nations High Commissioner for Human Rights, ProVeg International, Rainforest Action Network, Royal Society for the Protection of Birds, Stockholm Resilience Centre, The Nature Conservancy and United Nations Development Programme."},{"t":"8 CBD/COP/17/2, sub-item 17 (e)."},{"t":"9 Ibid., sub-item 18 (a)."},{"t":"10 CBD/COP/17/11."},{"t":"11 CBD/COP/17/INF/10."},{"t":"12 CBD/COP/17/INF/11."},{"t":"13 CBD/COP/17/1/Rev.1/Add.2/Rev.1-CBD/CP/MOP/12/1/Add.2/Rev.1, annex VI."},{"t":"4/15"}],"blocks":[{"md":"CBD/COP/17/WG.II/L.1-CBD/CP/MOP/12/WG.II/L.1","html":"<p>CBD/COP/17/WG.II/L.1-CBD/CP/MOP/12/WG.II/L.1</p>","en":[0]},{"md":"(e)","html":"<p>(e)</p>","pre":"P/MOP/12/WG.II/L.1\n\n","en":[0]},{"md":"與平台工作計畫相關之事項\n31. 第二工作小組於其第 1 次會議開始審議議程項目 17 (e)。其面前有一份決議草案。⁸\n32. 第二工作小組同意成立一個聯絡小組，由 Dickson Chitupa（辛巴威）與 Elif Skinner（英國）共同主持，其任務為就方括號文字達成共識，並定稿決議草案之文字。\n33.","html":"<p>與平台工作計畫相關之事項<br />\n31. 第二工作小組於其第 1 次會議開始審議議程項目 17 (e)。其面前有一份決議草案。⁸<br />\n32. 第二工作小組同意成立一個聯絡小組，由 Dickson Chitupa（辛巴威）與 Elif Skinner（英國）共同主持，其任務為就方括號文字達成共識，並定稿決議草案之文字。<br />\n33.</p>","en":[1,2,3]},{"md":"[待完成]","html":"<p>[待完成]</p>","en":[4]},{"md":"項目 18\n與實施昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要相關之其他科學與技術議題\n(a)","html":"<p>項目 18<br />\n與實施昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要相關之其他科學與技術議題<br />\n(a)</p>","en":[5,6,7]},{"md":"生物多樣性與氣候變遷\n34. 第二工作小組於其第 1 次會議開始審議議程項目 18 (a)。其面前有一份決議草案⁹ 以及秘書處關於生物多樣性與氣候變遷活動之進度報告¹⁰。此外，亦有兩份與子項目 18 (a) 相關之資訊文件發布：一份關於「氣候變遷調適與減災之生態系基礎方法設計與有效實施自願性指南」之擴充補充文件¹¹，以及一份關於「加強里約公約框架下合作、政策一致性與綜效之行動、差距與重疊之繪圖研究」¹²。\n35. 由於議程項目 18 (a) 已實施陳述書之提前提交機制¹³，即根據秘書處第 2026-072 號通知，在非正式且自願的基礎上提交陳述書，因此主席詢問附件 II（文件編號 CBD/COP/17/INF/24）所列之締約方與觀察員，是否反對其陳述書被視為針對本子項目正式提交之陳述書。現場未提出異議。\n36. 因此，第二工作小組同意下列締約方之陳述書應被視為於議程項目 18 (a) 下正式提交之陳述書：澳洲、孟加拉、巴西、加拿大、中國、象牙海岸、古巴、歐盟及其成員國、斐濟（代表太平洋小島嶼開發中國家）、瓜地馬拉、冰島、日本、約旦、馬達加斯加、馬爾地夫、摩洛哥、尼泊爾、紐西蘭、挪威、大韓民國、塞內加爾、蘇利南、瑞士與英國。\n37. 第二工作小組亦同意下列觀察員之陳述書應被視為於議程項目 18 (a) 下正式提交之陳述書：國際生物多樣性聯盟與國際熱帶農業研究中心（Alliance of Bioversity International and the International Center for Tropical Agriculture）、CGIAR、聯合國海洋事務及海洋法司、CBD 女性聯盟（CBD Women’s Caucus）、Exploring Womanhood Foundation、Fungi Foundation、全球青年生物多樣性網絡（Global Youth Biodiversity Network）、國際綠色和平（Greenpeace International）、美洲全球變遷研究中心（Inter-American Institute for Global Change Research）、國際商會（International Chamber of Commerce）、國際生物多樣性原住民族論壇（International Indigenous Forum on Biodiversity）、國際自然保護聯盟（IUCN）、聯合國人權事務高級專員辦事處、ProVeg International、雨林行動網絡（Rainforest Action Network）、皇家鳥類保護學會（Royal Society for the Protection of Birds）、斯德哥爾摩韌性中心（Stockholm Resilience Centre）、自然保護協會（The Nature Conservancy）以及聯合國開發計畫署（UNDP）。","html":"<p>生物多樣性與氣候變遷<br />\n34. 第二工作小組於其第 1 次會議開始審議議程項目 18 (a)。其面前有一份決議草案⁹ 以及秘書處關於生物多樣性與氣候變遷活動之進度報告¹⁰。此外，亦有兩份與子項目 18 (a) 相關之資訊文件發布：一份關於「氣候變遷調適與減災之生態系基礎方法設計與有效實施自願性指南」之擴充補充文件¹¹，以及一份關於「加強里約公約框架下合作、政策一致性與綜效之行動、差距與重疊之繪圖研究」¹²。<br />\n35. 由於議程項目 18 (a) 已實施陳述書之提前提交機制¹³，即根據秘書處第 2026-072 號通知，在非正式且自願的基礎上提交陳述書，因此主席詢問附件 II（文件編號 CBD/COP/17/INF/24）所列之締約方與觀察員，是否反對其陳述書被視為針對本子項目正式提交之陳述書。現場未提出異議。<br />\n36. 因此，第二工作小組同意下列締約方之陳述書應被視為於議程項目 18 (a) 下正式提交之陳述書：澳洲、孟加拉、巴西、加拿大、中國、象牙海岸、古巴、歐盟及其成員國、斐濟（代表太平洋小島嶼開發中國家）、瓜地馬拉、冰島、日本、約旦、馬達加斯加、馬爾地夫、摩洛哥、尼泊爾、紐西蘭、挪威、大韓民國、塞內加爾、蘇利南、瑞士與英國。<br />\n37. 第二工作小組亦同意下列觀察員之陳述書應被視為於議程項目 18 (a) 下正式提交之陳述書：國際生物多樣性聯盟與國際熱帶農業研究中心（Alliance of Bioversity International and the International Center for Tropical Agriculture）、CGIAR、聯合國海洋事務及海洋法司、CBD 女性聯盟（CBD Women’s Caucus）、Exploring Womanhood Foundation、Fungi Foundation、全球青年生物多樣性網絡（Global Youth Biodiversity Network）、國際綠色和平（Greenpeace International）、美洲全球變遷研究中心（Inter-American Institute for Global Change Research）、國際商會（International Chamber of Commerce）、國際生物多樣性原住民族論壇（International Indigenous Forum on Biodiversity）、國際自然保護聯盟（IUCN）、聯合國人權事務高級專員辦事處、ProVeg International、雨林行動網絡（Rainforest Action Network）、皇家鳥類保護學會（Royal Society for the Protection of Birds）、斯德哥爾摩韌性中心（Stockholm Resilience Centre）、自然保護協會（The Nature Conservancy）以及聯合國開發計畫署（UNDP）。</p>","en":[8,9,10,11,12]},{"md":"***\n⁸ CBD/COP/17/2，子項目 17 (e)。\n⁹ 同上，子項目 18 (a)。\n¹⁰ CBD/COP/17/11。\n¹¹ CBD/COP/17/INF/10。\n¹² CBD/COP/17/INF/11。\n¹³ CBD/COP/17/1/Rev.1/Add.2/Rev.1-CBD/CP/MOP/12/1/Add.2/Rev.1，附件 VI。","html":"<hr />\n<p>⁸ CBD/COP/17/2，子項目 17 (e)。<br />\n⁹ 同上，子項目 18 (a)。<br />\n¹⁰ CBD/COP/17/11。<br />\n¹¹ CBD/COP/17/INF/10。<br />\n¹² CBD/COP/17/INF/11。<br />\n¹³ CBD/COP/17/1/Rev.1/Add.2/Rev.1-CBD/CP/MOP/12/1/Add.2/Rev.1，附件 VI。</p>","en":[13,14,15,16,17]}]},{"p":"p005","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ae39ed27b12c517cf05e7cd/p005.md","en":[{"t":"CBD/COP/17/WG.II/L.1-CBD/CP/MOP/12/WG.II/L.1"},{"t":"38. In addition, statements were made in session by representatives of the following Parties: Argentina, Bahrain, Brazil, Cook Islands, India, Nigeria, Peru, South Africa (on behalf of the African States), Russian Federation, Saudi Arabia, Tuvalu (on behalf of the Pacific small island developing States), United Arab Emirates, United Kingdom and Zimbabwe."},{"t":"39. A statement was also made in session by a representative of the Global Youth Biodiversity Network."},{"t":"40. Working Group II agreed to establish a contact group, co-chaired by Clarisse Kehler Siebert (Sweden) and Xiang Gao (China), with the mandate to resolve the outstanding issues in the draft decision and to make any necessary changes in the light of the information provided in the progress report, basing its work on text prepared by the Chair with the assistance of the Secretariat."},{"t":"41. At its 8th session, Working Group II heard a report by one of the Co-Chairs of the contact group on the outcome of the group’s work."},{"t":"42.    [to be completed]"},{"t":"(b)    Sustainable wildlife management"},{"t":"43. Working Group II began its consideration of agenda item 18 (b) at its 1st session. It had before it a draft decision. 14 An information document containing a submission from the Collaborative Partnership on Sustainable Wildlife Management regarding sustainable wildlife management15 had also been issued in relation to sub-item 18 (b)."},{"t":"44. Working Group II agreed to establish a contact group, co-chaired by Lactitia Tshililo Tshitwamulomoni (South Africa) and Felix Lomans (Kingdom of the Netherlands), with the mandate to resolve the bracketed text in the draft decision."},{"t":"45. At its 8th session, Working Group II heard a report by one of the Co-Chairs of the contact group on the outcome of the group’s work."},{"t":"46.    [to be completed]"},{"t":"(c)    Marine and coastal biodiversity and island biodiversity"},{"t":"47. Working Group II began its consideration of agenda item 18 (c) at its 1st session. It had before it a draft decision.16"},{"t":"48. Working Group II agreed to establish a contact group, co-chaired by Patsy Nicole Contardo Urra (Chile) and Freydís Vigfúsdóttir (Iceland), with the mandate to resolve the bracketed text in the draft decision."},{"t":"49. At its 9th session, following a minute of silence to mark the passing of Piers Dunstan, Working Group II considered the revised draft decision submitted by the Chair."},{"t":"50. Statements were made by representatives of the following Parties: Australia, Canada, Chile, Colombia, Cook Islands (on behalf of the Pacific small island developing States), European Union and its member States, Iceland, Iran (Islamic Republic of), Jamaica, Norway, Panama, Peru, Philippines, Russian Federation, South Africa, Tuvalu and United Kingdom."},{"t":"51. Statements were also made by representatives of the CBD Women’s Caucus and the Global Youth Biodiversity Network."},{"t":"52.    [to be completed]"},{"t":"14 CBD/COP/17/2, sub-item 18 (b)."},{"t":"15 CBD/COP/17/INF/27."},{"t":"16 CBD/COP/17/2, sub-item 18 (c)."},{"t":"5/15"}],"blocks":[{"md":"CBD/COP/17/WG.II/L.1-CBD/CP/MOP/12/WG.II/L.1","html":"<p>CBD/COP/17/WG.II/L.1-CBD/CP/MOP/12/WG.II/L.1</p>","en":[0]},{"md":"38. 此外，下列締約方代表於會議中發表了聲明：\n阿根廷、巴林、巴西、庫克群島、印度、奈及利亞、秘魯、南非（代表非洲國家）、俄羅斯聯邦、沙烏地阿拉伯、吐瓦魯（代表太平洋小島嶼開發中國家）、阿拉伯聯合大公國、英國及辛巴威。\n39. 全球青年生物多樣性網絡（Global Youth Biodiversity Network）之代表亦於會議中發表了聲明。\n40. 第二工作小組同意成立一個聯絡小組，由 Clarisse Kehler Siebert（瑞典）與 Xiang Gao（中國）共同主持，其任務為解決決議草案中尚未解決的問題，並根據進度報告所提供的資訊進行任何必要的修改，其工作應以主席在秘書處協助下所準備之文本為基礎。\n41. 第二工作小組於其第 8 次會議中，聽取了聯絡小組其中一位共同主席關於該小組工作成果之報告。\n42.","html":"<p>38. 此外，下列締約方代表於會議中發表了聲明：<br />\n阿根廷、巴林、巴西、庫克群島、印度、奈及利亞、秘魯、南非（代表非洲國家）、俄羅斯聯邦、沙烏地阿拉伯、吐瓦魯（代表太平洋小島嶼開發中國家）、阿拉伯聯合大公國、英國及辛巴威。<br />\n39. 全球青年生物多樣性網絡（Global Youth Biodiversity Network）之代表亦於會議中發表了聲明。<br />\n40. 第二工作小組同意成立一個聯絡小組，由 Clarisse Kehler Siebert（瑞典）與 Xiang Gao（中國）共同主持，其任務為解決決議草案中尚未解決的問題，並根據進度報告所提供的資訊進行任何必要的修改，其工作應以主席在秘書處協助下所準備之文本為基礎。<br />\n41. 第二工作小組於其第 8 次會議中，聽取了聯絡小組其中一位共同主席關於該小組工作成果之報告。<br />\n42.</p>","en":[1,2,3,4]},{"md":"(b)","html":"<p>(b)</p>","pre":"席關於該小組工作成果之報告。\n42.\n\n","en":[5]},{"md":"[待完成]","html":"<p>[待完成]</p>","pre":"組工作成果之報告。\n42.\n\n(b)\n\n","en":[5]},{"md":"永續野生動物管理\n43. 第二工作小組於其第 1 次會議開始審議議程項目 18 (b)。其面前有一份決議草案。$^{14}$ 關於子項目 18 (b)，亦已發布一份包含永續野生動物管理合作夥伴關係（Collaborative Partnership on Sustainable Wildlife Management）就永續野生動物管理所提交之提案的資訊文件$^{15}$。\n44. 第二工作小組同意成立一個聯絡小組，由 Lactitia Tshililo Tshitwamulomoni（南非）與 Felix Lomans（荷蘭王國）共同主持，其任務為解決決議草案中的方括號文字。\n45. 第二工作小組於其第 8 次會議中，聽取了聯絡小組其中一位共同主席關於該小組工作成果之報告。\n46.","html":"<p>永續野生動物管理<br />\n43. 第二工作小組於其第 1 次會議開始審議議程項目 18 (b)。其面前有一份決議草案。<sup>14</sup> 關於子項目 18 (b)，亦已發布一份包含永續野生動物管理合作夥伴關係（Collaborative Partnership on Sustainable Wildlife Management）就永續野生動物管理所提交之提案的資訊文件<sup>15</sup>。<br />\n44. 第二工作小組同意成立一個聯絡小組，由 Lactitia Tshililo Tshitwamulomoni（南非）與 Felix Lomans（荷蘭王國）共同主持，其任務為解決決議草案中的方括號文字。<br />\n45. 第二工作小組於其第 8 次會議中，聽取了聯絡小組其中一位共同主席關於該小組工作成果之報告。<br />\n46.</p>","en":[6,7,8,9,10]},{"md":"(c)","html":"<p>(c)</p>","pre":"席關於該小組工作成果之報告。\n46.\n\n","en":[11]},{"md":"[待完成]","html":"<p>[待完成]</p>","pre":"組工作成果之報告。\n46.\n\n(c)\n\n","en":[11]},{"md":"海洋與沿岸生物多樣性及島嶼生物多樣性\n47. 第二工作小組於其第 1 次會議開始審議議程項目 18 (c)。其面前有一份決議草案$^{16}$。\n48. 第二工作小組同意成立一個聯絡小組，由 Patsy Nicole Contardo Urra（智利）與 Freydís Vigfúsdóttir（冰島）共同主持，其任務為解決決議草案中的方括弧文字。\n49. 第二工作小組於其第 9 次會議中，在進行悼念 Piers Dunstan 過世的默哀後，審議了由主席提交的修訂後決議草案。\n50. 下列締約方代表發表了聲明：澳洲、加拿大、智利、哥倫比亞、庫克群島（代表太平洋小島嶼開發中國家）、歐盟及其成員國、冰島、伊朗（伊斯蘭共和國）、牙買加、挪威、巴拿馬、秘魯、菲律賓、俄羅斯聯邦、南非、吐瓦魯及英國。\n51. CBD 女性聯盟（CBD Women’s Caucus）與全球青年生物多樣性網絡之代表亦發表了聲明。\n52.","html":"<p>海洋與沿岸生物多樣性及島嶼生物多樣性<br />\n47. 第二工作小組於其第 1 次會議開始審議議程項目 18 (c)。其面前有一份決議草案<sup>16</sup>。<br />\n48. 第二工作小組同意成立一個聯絡小組，由 Patsy Nicole Contardo Urra（智利）與 Freydís Vigfúsdóttir（冰島）共同主持，其任務為解決決議草案中的方括弧文字。<br />\n49. 第二工作小組於其第 9 次會議中，在進行悼念 Piers Dunstan 過世的默哀後，審議了由主席提交的修訂後決議草案。<br />\n50. 下列締約方代表發表了聲明：澳洲、加拿大、智利、哥倫比亞、庫克群島（代表太平洋小島嶼開發中國家）、歐盟及其成員國、冰島、伊朗（伊斯蘭共和國）、牙買加、挪威、巴拿馬、秘魯、菲律賓、俄羅斯聯邦、南非、吐瓦魯及英國。<br />\n51. CBD 女性聯盟（CBD Women’s Caucus）與全球青年生物多樣性網絡之代表亦發表了聲明。<br />\n52.</p>","en":[12,13,14,15,16]},{"md":"[待完成]","html":"<p>[待完成]</p>","pre":"樣性網絡之代表亦發表了聲明。\n52.\n\n","en":[17]},{"md":"$^{14}$ CBD/COP/17/2, 子項目 18 (b)。\n$^{15}$ CBD/COP/17/INF/27。\n$^{16}$ CBD/COP/17/2, 子項目 18 (c)。","html":"<p><sup>14</sup> CBD/COP/17/2, 子項目 18 (b)。<br />\n<sup>15</sup> CBD/COP/17/INF/27。<br />\n<sup>16</sup> CBD/COP/17/2, 子項目 18 (c)。</p>","en":[18,19,20,21]}]},{"p":"p006","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ae39ed27b12c517cf05e7cd/p006.md","en":[{"t":"CBD/COP/17/WG.II/L.1-CBD/CP/MOP/12/WG.II/L.1"},{"t":"(d)     Biodiversity and agriculture"},{"t":"53. Working Group II began its consideration of agenda item 18 (d) at its 1st session. It had before it a draft decision.17"},{"t":"54. The Chair said that he would conduct informal consultations as needed and prepare a revised version of the draft decision in consultation with the Secretariat."},{"t":"55. At its 7th session, on 23 October, Working Group II considered a draft decision submitted by the Chair."},{"t":"56. Statements were made by representatives of the following Parties: Argentina, Bahrain, Benin, Bhutan, Brazil, Cameroon, Canada, Colombia, Côte d’Ivoire, Democratic Republic of the Congo, European Union and its member States, Gabon, Guatemala, Iceland, India, Iran (Islamic Republic of), Japan, Mexico, Mongolia, Morocco, New Zealand, Norway, Panama, Philippines, Russian Federation, Saudi Arabia, Senegal, South Africa, Sri Lanka, Switzerland, United Kingdom, United Republic of Tanzania and Uruguay."},{"t":"57. The Chair established a group of friends of the Chair with the mandate to resolve the remaining issues in the draft decision."},{"t":"58. At its 8th session, following a report by a representative of Switzerland on the outcome of the work of the group of friends of the Chair, Working Group II resumed its consideration of the draft decision."},{"t":"59. Statements were made by representatives of the following Parties: Argentina, Brazil, Canada, European Union and its member States, India, New Zealand, Panama, Russian Federation, South Africa, Tuvalu and United Kingdom."},{"t":"60. Following the exchange of views, Working Group II agreed that the Chair would prepare a revised version of the draft decision."},{"t":"61.     At its 10th session, Working Group II considered a draft decision submitted by the Chair."},{"t":"62. Statements were made by representatives of the following Parties: Argentina, Australia, Bangladesh, Brazil, Canada, European Union and its member States, India, Morocco, Norway, Russian Federation, South Africa, Switzerland, United Kingdom and Uruguay."},{"t":"63. Working Group II approved the draft decision, as orally amended, for transmission to the plenary session as draft decision CBD/COP/17/L.xx."},{"t":"(e)     Invasive alien species"},{"t":"64. Working Group II began its consideration of agenda item 18 (e) at its 1st session. It had before it a draft decision.18"},{"t":"65. The Chair said that he would conduct informal consultations as needed and prepare a revised version of the draft decision in consultation with the Secretariat."},{"t":"66. At its 4th session, Working Group II began its consideration of a draft decision submitted by the Chair."},{"t":"67. Statements were made by representatives of the following Parties: Argentina, Benin, Brazil, Cameroon, Chile, Cook Islands (on behalf of the Pacific small island developing States), Costa Rica, Côte d’Ivoire, Cuba, Democratic Republic of the Congo, European Union and its member States, Guatemala, India, Indonesia, Japan, Kyrgyzstan, Mexico, Mongolia, Norway, Panama, Russian Federation, Samoa, Senegal, South Africa, Switzerland, Türkiye, United Kingdom and Uruguay."},{"t":"17 Ibid., sub-item 18 (d)."},{"t":"18 Ibid., sub-item 18 (e)."},{"t":"6/15"}],"blocks":[{"md":"CBD/COP/17/WG.II/L.1-CBD/CP/MOP/12/WG.II/L.1","html":"<p>CBD/COP/17/WG.II/L.1-CBD/CP/MOP/12/WG.II/L.1</p>","en":[0,1,2]},{"md":"(d)","html":"<p>(d)</p>","pre":"P/MOP/12/WG.II/L.1\n\n","en":[]},{"md":"生物多樣性與農業\n53. 第二工作小組於其第 1 次會議開始審議議程項目 18 (d)。其面前有一份決議草案.17\n54. 主席表示，他將視需要進行非正式諮商，並與秘書處協商以準備決議草案的修訂版本。\n55. 在其第 7 次會議（10 月 23 日）期間，第二工作小組審議了由主席提交的決議草案。\n56. 以下締約方代表發表了聲明：阿根廷、巴林、貝南、不丹、巴西、喀麥隆、加拿大、哥倫比亞、象牙海岸、剛果民主共和國、歐盟及其成員國、加彭、瓜地馬拉、冰島、印度、伊朗（伊斯蘭共和國）、日本、墨西哥、蒙古、摩洛哥、紐西蘭、挪威、巴拿馬、菲律賓、俄羅斯聯邦、沙烏地阿拉伯、塞內加爾、南非、斯里蘭卡、瑞士、英國、坦尚尼亞聯合共和國及烏拉圭。\n57. 主席成立了一個主席之友小組，其任務是解決決議草案中剩餘的問題。\n58. 在其第 8 次會議期間，在瑞士代表就主席之友小組的工作成果發表報告後，第二工作小組恢復審議該決議草案。\n59. 以下締約方代表發表了聲明：阿根廷、巴西、加拿大、歐盟及其成員國、印度、紐西蘭、巴拿馬、俄羅斯聯邦、南非、吐瓦魯及英國。\n60. 在意見交換後，第二工作小組同意由主席準備決議草案的修訂版本。\n61. 在其第 10 次會議期間，第二工作小組審議了由主席提交的決議草案。\n62. 以下締約方代表發表了聲明：阿根廷、澳洲、孟加拉、巴西、加拿大、歐盟及其成員國、印度、摩洛哥、挪威、俄羅斯聯邦、南非、瑞士、英國及烏拉圭。\n63. 第二工作小組通過了經口頭修正的決議草案，並將其作為決議草案 CBD/COP/17/L.xx 提交全會。","html":"<p>生物多樣性與農業<br />\n53. 第二工作小組於其第 1 次會議開始審議議程項目 18 (d)。其面前有一份決議草案.17<br />\n54. 主席表示，他將視需要進行非正式諮商，並與秘書處協商以準備決議草案的修訂版本。<br />\n55. 在其第 7 次會議（10 月 23 日）期間，第二工作小組審議了由主席提交的決議草案。<br />\n56. 以下締約方代表發表了聲明：阿根廷、巴林、貝南、不丹、巴西、喀麥隆、加拿大、哥倫比亞、象牙海岸、剛果民主共和國、歐盟及其成員國、加彭、瓜地馬拉、冰島、印度、伊朗（伊斯蘭共和國）、日本、墨西哥、蒙古、摩洛哥、紐西蘭、挪威、巴拿馬、菲律賓、俄羅斯聯邦、沙烏地阿拉伯、塞內加爾、南非、斯里蘭卡、瑞士、英國、坦尚尼亞聯合共和國及烏拉圭。<br />\n57. 主席成立了一個主席之友小組，其任務是解決決議草案中剩餘的問題。<br />\n58. 在其第 8 次會議期間，在瑞士代表就主席之友小組的工作成果發表報告後，第二工作小組恢復審議該決議草案。<br />\n59. 以下締約方代表發表了聲明：阿根廷、巴西、加拿大、歐盟及其成員國、印度、紐西蘭、巴拿馬、俄羅斯聯邦、南非、吐瓦魯及英國。<br />\n60. 在意見交換後，第二工作小組同意由主席準備決議草案的修訂版本。<br />\n61. 在其第 10 次會議期間，第二工作小組審議了由主席提交的決議草案。<br />\n62. 以下締約方代表發表了聲明：阿根廷、澳洲、孟加拉、巴西、加拿大、歐盟及其成員國、印度、摩洛哥、挪威、俄羅斯聯邦、南非、瑞士、英國及烏拉圭。<br />\n63. 第二工作小組通過了經口頭修正的決議草案，並將其作為決議草案 CBD/COP/17/L.xx 提交全會。</p>","en":[3,4,5,6,7]},{"md":"(e)","html":"<p>(e)</p>","pre":"/COP/17/L.xx 提交全會。\n\n","en":[8,9,10,11,12]},{"md":"外來入侵種\n64. 第二工作小組於其第 1 次會議開始審議議程項目 18 (e)。其面前有一份決議草案.18\n65. 主席表示，他將視需要進行非正式諮商，並與秘書處協商以準備決議草案的修訂版本。\n66. 在其第 4 次會議期間，第二工作小組開始審議由主席提交的決議草案。\n67. 以下締約方代表發表了聲明：阿根廷、貝南、巴西、喀麥隆、智利、庫克群島（代表太平洋小島嶼開發中國家）、哥斯大黎加、象牙海岸、古巴、剛果民主共和國、歐盟及其成員國、瓜地馬拉、印度、印尼、日本、吉爾吉斯、墨西哥、蒙古、挪威、巴拿馬、俄羅斯聯邦、薩摩亞、塞內加爾、南非、瑞士、土耳其、英國及烏拉圭。","html":"<p>外來入侵種<br />\n64. 第二工作小組於其第 1 次會議開始審議議程項目 18 (e)。其面前有一份決議草案.18<br />\n65. 主席表示，他將視需要進行非正式諮商，並與秘書處協商以準備決議草案的修訂版本。<br />\n66. 在其第 4 次會議期間，第二工作小組開始審議由主席提交的決議草案。<br />\n67. 以下締約方代表發表了聲明：阿根廷、貝南、巴西、喀麥隆、智利、庫克群島（代表太平洋小島嶼開發中國家）、哥斯大黎加、象牙海岸、古巴、剛果民主共和國、歐盟及其成員國、瓜地馬拉、印度、印尼、日本、吉爾吉斯、墨西哥、蒙古、挪威、巴拿馬、俄羅斯聯邦、薩摩亞、塞內加爾、南非、瑞士、土耳其、英國及烏拉圭。</p>","en":[13,14,15,16,17]},{"md":"17 同前引，子項目 18 (d)。\n18 同前引，子項目 18 (e)。","html":"<p>17 同前引，子項目 18 (d)。<br />\n18 同前引，子項目 18 (e)。</p>","en":[18,19,20]}]},{"p":"p007","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ae39ed27b12c517cf05e7cd/p007.md","en":[{"t":"CBD/COP/17/WG.II/L.1-CBD/CP/MOP/12/WG.II/L.1"},{"t":"68. The Working Group agreed that interested Parties would hold informal discussions with a view to resolving the remaining issues."},{"t":"69. At its 6th session, on 22 October, Working Group II resumed its consideration of the draft decision."},{"t":"70. The representative of the United Kingdom reported that the informal discussions had not yet concluded."},{"t":"71. Statements were made by representatives of the following Parties: Argentina, Brazil, Canada, Cook Islands (on behalf of the Pacific small island developing States), Egypt, European Union and its member States, Fiji, Indonesia, Morocco, Panama, Russian Federation, South Africa, State of Palestine, Tuvalu, United Kingdom and Viet Nam."},{"t":"72. Working Group II approved the draft decision, as orally amended, for transmission to the plenary session as draft decision CBD/COP/17/L.5."},{"t":"73.      [to be completed]"},{"t":"(f)     Biodiversity and health"},{"t":"74. Working Group II began its consideration of agenda item 18 (f) at its 1st session. It had before it a draft decision19 and a progress report by the Secretariat on activities on biodiversity and health.20 The following information documents had also been issued in relation to sub-item 18 (f): a note by the Secretariat on steps and process for the development of science-based indicators, metrics and progress measurement tools on biodiversity and health,21 a compilation of existing indicators relevant to biodiversity and health from other processes,22 a document on a framework and methodology for indicators on biodiversity and health 23 and a note by the Secretariat on an operational tool for indicators on biodiversity and health.24"},{"t":"75. As the modalities for the early submission of statements had been implemented for agenda item 18 (f), with statements submitted on an informal and voluntary basis pursuant to notification No. 2026-072, the Chair asked the Parties and observers listed in annex III to document CBD/COP/17/INF/24 and present at the session whether they objected to their statements being considered as statements officially submitted for the present sub-item. No objections were raised."},{"t":"76. Working Group II therefore agreed that the statements of the following Parties be considered as statements officially submitted under agenda item 18 (f): Bangladesh, Brazil, Côte d’Ivoire, Cuba, European Union and its member States, Fiji (on behalf of the Pacific small island developing States), Guatemala, Japan, Madagascar, Morocco, Norway, Senegal, Switzerland and United Kingdom."},{"t":"77. Working Group II also agreed that the statements of the following observers be considered as statements officially submitted under agenda item 18 (f): Alliance of Bioversity International and International Center for Tropical Agriculture, Born Free Foundation, CBD Women’s Caucus, Co-operation on Health and Biodiversity Initiative Secretariat, Global Youth Biodiversity Network, ICLEI – Local Governments for Sustainability, International Indigenous Forum on Biodiversity, International Union for Conservation of Nature and World Wide Fund for Nature International."},{"t":"78. In addition, statements were made in session by representatives of the following Parties: Argentina, Bahrain, Bangladesh, China, Cook Islands, Guatemala, India, Indonesia, Russian Federation, South Africa and Vanuatu (on behalf of the Pacific small island developing States)."},{"t":"19 Ibid., sub-item 18 (f)."},{"t":"20 CBD/COP/17/7."},{"t":"21 CBD/COP/17/INF/5."},{"t":"22 CBD/COP/17/INF/6."},{"t":"23 CBD/COP/17/INF/8."},{"t":"24 CBD/COP/17/INF/9 and its annex."},{"t":"7/15"}],"blocks":[{"md":"CBD/COP/17/WG.II/L.1-CBD/CP/MOP/12/WG.II/L.1","html":"<p>CBD/COP/17/WG.II/L.1-CBD/CP/MOP/12/WG.II/L.1</p>","en":[0,1]},{"md":"68. 工作小組同意，感興趣的締約方將進行非正式討論，以期解決剩餘議題。\n69. 在其第 6 次會議中，於 10 月 22 日，第二工作小組恢復對決議草案的審議。\n70. 英國代表報告，非正式討論尚未結束。\n71. 以下締約方代表發表了聲明：阿根廷、巴西、加拿大、庫克群島（代表太平洋小島嶼開發中國家）、埃及、歐盟及其成員國、斐濟、印尼、摩洛哥、巴拿馬、俄羅斯聯邦、南非、巴勒斯坦國、吐瓦魯、英國及越南。\n72. 第二工作小組通過經口頭修正後的決議草案，並將其作為決議草案 CBD/COP/17/L.5 送交全體會議。\n73.","html":"<p>68. 工作小組同意，感興趣的締約方將進行非正式討論，以期解決剩餘議題。<br />\n69. 在其第 6 次會議中，於 10 月 22 日，第二工作小組恢復對決議草案的審議。<br />\n70. 英國代表報告，非正式討論尚未結束。<br />\n71. 以下締約方代表發表了聲明：阿根廷、巴西、加拿大、庫克群島（代表太平洋小島嶼開發中國家）、埃及、歐盟及其成員國、斐濟、印尼、摩洛哥、巴拿馬、俄羅斯聯邦、南非、巴勒斯坦國、吐瓦魯、英國及越南。<br />\n72. 第二工作小組通過經口頭修正後的決議草案，並將其作為決議草案 CBD/COP/17/L.5 送交全體會議。<br />\n73.</p>","en":[2,3,4,5,6]},{"md":"(f)","html":"<p>(f)</p>","pre":"17/L.5 送交全體會議。\n73.\n\n","en":[7]},{"md":"[待完成]","html":"<p>[待完成]</p>","en":[7]},{"md":"生物多樣性與健康\n74. 第二工作小組於其第 1 次會議開始審議議程項目 18 (f)。其面前有一份決議草案$^{19}$以及秘書處關於生物多樣性與健康活動的進度報告$^{20}$。與子項目 18 (f) 相關的資訊文件還包括：秘書處關於開發以科學為基礎的生物多樣性與健康指標、度量標準及進度衡量工具之步驟與程序的說明$^{21}$、彙編自其他程序中與生物多樣性與健康相關之現有指標$^{22}$、關於生物多樣性與健康指標之架構與方法論的文件$^{23}$，以及秘書處關於生物多樣性與健康指標之操作工具的說明$^{24}$。\n75. 由於議程項目 18 (f) 已實施聲明提早提交之模式，即根據第 2026-072 號通知，在非正式且自願的基礎上提交聲明，因此主席要求附件 III（文件編號 CBD/COP/17/INF/24）所列之締約方與觀察員，於會議期間說明是否反對其聲明被視為針對本子項目正式提交之聲明。無人提出異議。\n76. 因此，第二工作小組同意將以下締約方的聲明視為在議程項目 18 (f) 下正式提交之聲明：孟加拉、巴西、象牙海岸、古巴、歐盟及其成員國、斐濟（代表太平洋小島嶼開發中國家）、瓜地馬拉、日本、馬達加斯加、摩洛哥、挪威、塞內加爾、瑞士及英國。\n77. 第二工作小組亦同意將以下觀察員的聲明視為在議程項目 18 (f) 下正式提交之聲明：國際生物多樣性聯盟與國際熱帶農業中心（Alliance of Bioversity International and International Center for Tropical Agriculture）、自由誕生基金會（Born Free Foundation）、CBD 女性聯盟（CBD Women’s Caucus）、健康與生物多樣性合作倡議秘書處（Cooperation on Health and Biodiversity Initiative Secretariat）、全球青年生物多樣性網絡（Global Youth Biodiversity Network）、ICLEI－地方政府永續發展聯盟（ICLEI – Local Governments for \nSustainability）、國際生物多樣性原住民族論壇（International Indigenous Forum on Biodiversity）、國際自然保護聯盟（International Union for Conservation of Nature）及世界自然基金會國際事務處（World Wide Fund for Nature International）。\n78. 此外，以下締約方代表在會議期間發表了聲明：阿根廷、巴林、孟加拉、中國、庫克群島、瓜地馬拉、印度、印尼、俄羅斯聯邦、南非及萬那杜（代表太平洋小島嶼開發中國家）。","html":"<p>生物多樣性與健康<br />\n74. 第二工作小組於其第 1 次會議開始審議議程項目 18 (f)。其面前有一份決議草案<sup>19</sup>以及秘書處關於生物多樣性與健康活動的進度報告<sup>20</sup>。與子項目 18 (f) 相關的資訊文件還包括：秘書處關於開發以科學為基礎的生物多樣性與健康指標、度量標準及進度衡量工具之步驟與程序的說明<sup>21</sup>、彙編自其他程序中與生物多樣性與健康相關之現有指標<sup>22</sup>、關於生物多樣性與健康指標之架構與方法論的文件<sup>23</sup>，以及秘書處關於生物多樣性與健康指標之操作工具的說明<sup>24</sup>。<br />\n75. 由於議程項目 18 (f) 已實施聲明提早提交之模式，即根據第 2026-072 號通知，在非正式且自願的基礎上提交聲明，因此主席要求附件 III（文件編號 CBD/COP/17/INF/24）所列之締約方與觀察員，於會議期間說明是否反對其聲明被視為針對本子項目正式提交之聲明。無人提出異議。<br />\n76. 因此，第二工作小組同意將以下締約方的聲明視為在議程項目 18 (f) 下正式提交之聲明：孟加拉、巴西、象牙海岸、古巴、歐盟及其成員國、斐濟（代表太平洋小島嶼開發中國家）、瓜地馬拉、日本、馬達加斯加、摩洛哥、挪威、塞內加爾、瑞士及英國。<br />\n77. 第二工作小組亦同意將以下觀察員的聲明視為在議程項目 18 (f) 下正式提交之聲明：國際生物多樣性聯盟與國際熱帶農業中心（Alliance of Bioversity International and International Center for Tropical Agriculture）、自由誕生基金會（Born Free Foundation）、CBD 女性聯盟（CBD Women’s Caucus）、健康與生物多樣性合作倡議秘書處（Cooperation on Health and Biodiversity Initiative Secretariat）、全球青年生物多樣性網絡（Global Youth Biodiversity Network）、ICLEI－地方政府永續發展聯盟（ICLEI – Local Governments for <br />\nSustainability）、國際生物多樣性原住民族論壇（International Indigenous Forum on Biodiversity）、國際自然保護聯盟（International Union for Conservation of Nature）及世界自然基金會國際事務處（World Wide Fund for Nature International）。<br />\n78. 此外，以下締約方代表在會議期間發表了聲明：阿根廷、巴林、孟加拉、中國、庫克群島、瓜地馬拉、印度、印尼、俄羅斯聯邦、南非及萬那杜（代表太平洋小島嶼開發中國家）。</p>","en":[8,9,10,11,12]},{"md":"$^{19}$ 同上，子項目 18 (f)。\n$^{20}$ CBD/COP/17/7。\n$^{21}$ CBD/COP/17/INF/5。\n$^{22}$ CBD/COP/17/INF/6。\n$^{23}$ CBD/COP/17/INF/8。\n$^{24}$ CBD/COP/17/INF/9 及其附件。","html":"<p><sup>19</sup> 同上，子項目 18 (f)。<br />\n<sup>20</sup> CBD/COP/17/7。<br />\n<sup>21</sup> CBD/COP/17/INF/5。<br />\n<sup>22</sup> CBD/COP/17/INF/6。<br />\n<sup>23</sup> CBD/COP/17/INF/8。<br />\n<sup>24</sup> CBD/COP/17/INF/9 及其附件。</p>","en":[14,15,16,17,18]}]},{"p":"p008","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ae39ed27b12c517cf05e7cd/p008.md","en":[{"t":"CBD/COP/17/WG.II/L.1-CBD/CP/MOP/12/WG.II/L.1"},{"t":"79. A statement was also made in session by a representative of the Secretariat of the Convention on International Trade in Endangered Species of Wild Fauna and Flora."},{"t":"80. A statement was further made in session by a representative of the Global Youth Biodiversity Network."},{"t":"81. Working Group II agreed to establish a contact group, co-chaired by Barbara Engels (Germany) and Kishma Primus-Ormond (Antigua and Barbuda), with the mandate to resolve the bracketed text in the draft decision, making changes only on the basis of the progress report and basing its work on text prepared by the Chair with the assistance of the Secretariat."},{"t":"82. At the 7th session, one of the Co-Chairs of the contact group reported on the outcome of the group’s work and indicated that the Co-Chairs had convened a small group to help them to find common ground on the remaining issues."},{"t":"83. The Chair said that he would prepare a revised version of the draft decision in consultation with the Secretariat and the contact group Co-Chairs."},{"t":"84. At its 8th session, Working Group II heard a report by one of the Co-Chairs of the contact group on the outcome of the discussions held in the small group."},{"t":"85.   [to be completed]"},{"t":"II. Twelfth meeting of the Conference of the Parties to the Convention"},{"t":"on Biological Diversity serving as the meeting of the Parties to the"},{"t":"Cartagena Protocol"},{"t":"Item 5"},{"t":"Report of the Compliance Committee"},{"t":"86. Working Group II began its consideration of agenda item 5 at its 2nd session, on 20 October. It had before it a draft decision,25 as well as the report of the Compliance Committee under the Cartagena Protocol on Biosafety on its twentieth and twenty-first meetings.26"},{"t":"87.   The Chair of the Compliance Committee presented the Committee’s report."},{"t":"88. As the modalities for the early submission of statements had been applied to agenda item 5, with statements submitted pursuant to notification No. 2026-072, the Chair asked the Parties listed in annex I to document CBD/CP/MOP/12/INF/8 and present at the session whether they objected to their statements being considered as statements officially submitted for the present item. No objections were raised."},{"t":"89. Working Group II therefore agreed that the statements of the following Parties be considered as statements officially submitted under agenda item 5: Brazil, Chad, Côte d’Ivoire, European Union and its member States, Japan, Norway and Switzerland."},{"t":"90. The Chair said that he would prepare a revised version of the draft decision in consultation with the Secretariat, taking into account the views expressed or supported by Parties."},{"t":"91.   At its 5th session, on 22 October, Working Group II considered a draft decision submitted by the Chair."},{"t":"92. Working Group II approved the draft decision for transmission to the plenary session as draft decision CBD/CP/MOP/12/L.2."},{"t":"25 CBD/CP/MOP/12/2, item 5."},{"t":"26 CBD/CP/MOP/12/3."},{"t":"8/15"}],"blocks":[{"md":"CBD/COP/17/WG.II/L.1-CBD/CP/MOP/12/WG.II/L.1","html":"<p>CBD/COP/17/WG.II/L.1-CBD/CP/MOP/12/WG.II/L.1</p>","en":[0,1]},{"md":"79. 會議期間，瀕危野生動植物種國際貿易公約（CITES）秘書處代表亦發表了聲明。\n80. 會議期間，全球青年生物多樣性網絡（Global Youth Biodiversity Network）代表亦進一步發表了聲明。\n81. 第二工作小組同意成立一個聯絡小組，由 Barbara Engels（德國）與 Kishma Primus-Ormond（安地卡及巴布達）共同主持，其任務為解決決議草案中的方括號文字，且僅能根據進度報告進行修改，並在其工作基礎上使用由主席在秘書處協助下所準備之文字。\n82. 在第七次會議中，聯絡小組的一位共同主席報告了該小組工作成果，並指出共同主席已召集一個小組，以協助其針對剩餘議題尋求共同點。\n83. 主席表示，他將與秘書處及聯絡小組共同主席協商，準備一份修訂後的決議草案版本。\n84. 在第八次會議中，第二工作小組聽取了聯絡小組其中一位共同主席關於小組內進行討論之成果報告。\n85.","html":"<p>79. 會議期間，瀕危野生動植物種國際貿易公約（CITES）秘書處代表亦發表了聲明。<br />\n80. 會議期間，全球青年生物多樣性網絡（Global Youth Biodiversity Network）代表亦進一步發表了聲明。<br />\n81. 第二工作小組同意成立一個聯絡小組，由 Barbara Engels（德國）與 Kishma Primus-Ormond（安地卡及巴布達）共同主持，其任務為解決決議草案中的方括號文字，且僅能根據進度報告進行修改，並在其工作基礎上使用由主席在秘書處協助下所準備之文字。<br />\n82. 在第七次會議中，聯絡小組的一位共同主席報告了該小組工作成果，並指出共同主席已召集一個小組，以協助其針對剩餘議題尋求共同點。<br />\n83. 主席表示，他將與秘書處及聯絡小組共同主席協商，準備一份修訂後的決議草案版本。<br />\n84. 在第八次會議中，第二工作小組聽取了聯絡小組其中一位共同主席關於小組內進行討論之成果報告。<br />\n85.</p>","en":[2,3,4,5,6]},{"md":"[待完成]","html":"<p>[待完成]</p>","en":[7,8]},{"md":"II. 生物多樣性公約締約方大會第十二次會議，同時作為卡塔赫納生物安全議定書締約方會議\n議程第 5 項\n遵從委員會報告\n86. 第二工作小組於 10 月 20 日的第二次會議開始審議議程第 5 項。其面前有一份決議草案，$^{25}$ 以及卡塔赫納生物安全議定書下遵從委員會於第二十次及第二十一次會議之報告。$^{26}$\n87. 遵從委員會主席提交了委員會報告。","html":"<p>II. 生物多樣性公約締約方大會第十二次會議，同時作為卡塔赫納生物安全議定書締約方會議<br />\n議程第 5 項<br />\n遵從委員會報告<br />\n86. 第二工作小組於 10 月 20 日的第二次會議開始審議議程第 5 項。其面前有一份決議草案，<sup>25</sup> 以及卡塔赫納生物安全議定書下遵從委員會於第二十次及第二十一次會議之報告。<sup>26</sup><br />\n87. 遵從委員會主席提交了委員會報告。</p>","en":[9,10,11,12,13]},{"md":"88. 由於議程第 5 項已適用提前提交聲明的程序，且聲明係根據通知編號 2026-072 提交，主席詢問附件 I 所列之締約方（文件編號 CBD/CP/MOP/12/INF/8）在本次會議中，是否反對其聲明被視為針對本議程正式提交之聲明。無人提出異議。\n89. 因此，第二工作小組同意將下列締約方之聲明視為依議程第 5 項正式提交之聲明：巴西、查德、象牙海岸、歐盟及其成員國、日本、挪威及瑞士。\n90. 主席表示，他將與秘書處協商，並考慮締約方所表達或支持之意見，準備一份修訂後的決議草案版本。\n91. 在 10 月 22 日的第五次會議中，第二工作小組審議了由主席提交的決議草案。\n92. 第二工作小組通過該決議草案，並將其提交全會，作為決議草案 CBD/CP/MOP/12/L.2。","html":"<p>88. 由於議程第 5 項已適用提前提交聲明的程序，且聲明係根據通知編號 2026-072 提交，主席詢問附件 I 所列之締約方（文件編號 CBD/CP/MOP/12/INF/8）在本次會議中，是否反對其聲明被視為針對本議程正式提交之聲明。無人提出異議。<br />\n89. 因此，第二工作小組同意將下列締約方之聲明視為依議程第 5 項正式提交之聲明：巴西、查德、象牙海岸、歐盟及其成員國、日本、挪威及瑞士。<br />\n90. 主席表示，他將與秘書處協商，並考慮締約方所表達或支持之意見，準備一份修訂後的決議草案版本。<br />\n91. 在 10 月 22 日的第五次會議中，第二工作小組審議了由主席提交的決議草案。<br />\n92. 第二工作小組通過該決議草案，並將其提交全會，作為決議草案 CBD/CP/MOP/12/L.2。</p>","en":[14,15,16,17,18]},{"md":"$^{25}$ CBD/CP/MOP/12/2，第 5 項。\n$^{26}$ CBD/CP/MOP/12/3。","html":"<p><sup>25</sup> CBD/CP/MOP/12/2，第 5 項。<br />\n<sup>26</sup> CBD/CP/MOP/12/3。</p>","en":[19,20,21,22]}]},{"p":"p009","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ae39ed27b12c517cf05e7cd/p009.md","en":[{"t":"CBD/COP/17/WG.II/L.1-CBD/CP/MOP/12/WG.II/L.1"},{"t":"Item 7"},{"t":"Monitoring and reporting"},{"t":"93. Working Group II began its consideration of agenda item 7 at its 2nd session. It had before it a draft decision,27 as well as a note by the Secretariat on monitoring and reporting.28"},{"t":"94. As the modalities for the early submission of statements had been implemented for agenda item 7, with statements submitted pursuant to notification No. 2026-072, the Chair asked the Parties listed in annex II to document CBD/CP/MOP/12/INF/8 and present at the session whether they objected to their statements being considered as statements officially submitted for the present item. No objections were raised."},{"t":"95. Working Group II therefore agreed that the statements of the following Parties be considered as statements officially submitted under agenda item 7: Colombia, Côte d’Ivoire, European Union and its member States, Japan, Jordan, Norway and Switzerland."},{"t":"96. In addition, statements were made in session by representatives of the following Parties: Kenya (on behalf of the African group), Malawi and South Africa."},{"t":"97. Following the exchange of views, the Chair said that he would prepare a revised version of the draft decision in consultation with the Secretariat, taking into account the views expressed or supported by Parties."},{"t":"98.    At its 5th session, Working Group II considered a draft decision submitted by the Chair."},{"t":"99. Statements were made by representatives of the following Parties: European Union and its member States and Kenya (on behalf of the African States)."},{"t":"100. Working Group II approved the draft decision, as orally amended, for transmission to the plenary session as draft decision CBD/CP/MOP/12/L.6."},{"t":"Item 8"},{"t":"Assessment and review of the effectiveness of the Cartagena Protocol and midterm evaluation of the implementation plan and capacity-building action plan for the Protocol"},{"t":"101. Working Group II began its consideration of agenda item 8 at its 1st session. It had before it a draft decision.29 A note by the Secretariat on an analysis of information for the fifth assessment and review of the effectiveness of the Cartagena Protocol on Biosafety and midterm evaluation of the implementation plan and capacity-building action plan for the Protocol 30 had also been made available as a reference document."},{"t":"102. A statement was made by a representative of Panama."},{"t":"103. The Chair said that he would conduct informal consultations as needed and prepare a revised version of the draft decision in consultation with the Secretariat."},{"t":"104. At its 6th session, Working Group II considered a draft decision submitted by the Chair."},{"t":"105. Statements were made by representatives of the following Parties: Benin, Brazil, Côte d’Ivoire, Egypt, European Union and its member States, Fiji (on behalf of the Pacific small island developing States), India, Japan, Malawi, Morocco, New Zealand, Nigeria, Norway, Panama, Paraguay, Philippines, Senegal, State of Palestine and United Kingdom."},{"t":"106. Working Group II agreed to resume its consideration of the draft decision at a later session following informal discussions."},{"t":"27 CBD/CP/MOP/12/2, item 7."},{"t":"28 CBD/CP/MOP/12/6."},{"t":"29 CBD/CP/MOP/12/2, item 8."},{"t":"30 CBD/SBI/7/6/Add.1."},{"t":"9/15"}],"blocks":[{"md":"CBD/COP/17/WG.II/L.1-CBD/CP/MOP/12/WG.II/L.1","html":"<p>CBD/COP/17/WG.II/L.1-CBD/CP/MOP/12/WG.II/L.1</p>","en":[0,1,2,3]},{"md":"議程項目 7\n監測與報告\n93. 第二工作小組於其第二次會議開始審議議程項目 7。其面前有一份決議草案，$^{27}$ 以及秘書處關於監測與報告的說明。$^{28}$\n94. 由於議程項目 7 已實施提早提交聲明的程序，且聲明係根據通知編號 2026-072 提交，因此主席要求附件 II 中列出的締約方（見 CBD/CP/MOP/12/INF/8）於會議期間說明，是否反對其聲明被視為針對本項目正式提交的聲明。無人提出異議。\n95. 因此，第二工作小組同意將下列締約方的聲明視為根據議程項目 7 正式提交的聲明：哥倫比亞、象牙海岸、歐盟及其成員國、日本、約旦、挪威及瑞士。\n96. 此外，下列締約方代表於會議中發表了聲明：肯亞（代表非洲集團）、馬拉威及南非。\n97. 在意見交換後，主席表示他將諮詢秘書處，並考量締約方所表達或支持的意見，準備一份修訂後的決議草案版本。\n98. 第二工作小組於其第五次會議審議由主席提交的決議草案。\n99. 下列締約方代表發表了聲明：歐盟及其成員國，以及肯亞（代表非洲國家）。\n100. 第二工作小組通過經口頭修正後的決議草案，並將其作為決議草案 CBD/CP/MOP/12/L.6 提交全會。","html":"<p>議程項目 7<br />\n監測與報告<br />\n93. 第二工作小組於其第二次會議開始審議議程項目 7。其面前有一份決議草案，<sup>27</sup> 以及秘書處關於監測與報告的說明。<sup>28</sup><br />\n94. 由於議程項目 7 已實施提早提交聲明的程序，且聲明係根據通知編號 2026-072 提交，因此主席要求附件 II 中列出的締約方（見 CBD/CP/MOP/12/INF/8）於會議期間說明，是否反對其聲明被視為針對本項目正式提交的聲明。無人提出異議。<br />\n95. 因此，第二工作小組同意將下列締約方的聲明視為根據議程項目 7 正式提交的聲明：哥倫比亞、象牙海岸、歐盟及其成員國、日本、約旦、挪威及瑞士。<br />\n96. 此外，下列締約方代表於會議中發表了聲明：肯亞（代表非洲集團）、馬拉威及南非。<br />\n97. 在意見交換後，主席表示他將諮詢秘書處，並考量締約方所表達或支持的意見，準備一份修訂後的決議草案版本。<br />\n98. 第二工作小組於其第五次會議審議由主席提交的決議草案。<br />\n99. 下列締約方代表發表了聲明：歐盟及其成員國，以及肯亞（代表非洲國家）。<br />\n100. 第二工作小組通過經口頭修正後的決議草案，並將其作為決議草案 CBD/CP/MOP/12/L.6 提交全會。</p>","en":[4,5,6,7,8]},{"md":"議程項目 8\n卡塔赫納生物安全議定書有效性之評估與審查，以及議定書執行計畫與能力建構行動計畫之中期評估\n101. 第二工作小組於其第一次會議開始審議議程項目 8。其面前有一份決議草案。$^{29}$ 此外，秘書處關於卡塔赫納生物安全議定書有效性第五次評估與審查，以及議定書執行計畫與能力建構行動計畫之中期評估之資訊分析說明$^{30}$，亦已作為參考文件提供。\n102. 巴拿馬代表發表了聲明。\n103. 主席表示，他將視需要進行非正式諮商，並諮詢秘書處以準備一份修訂後的決議草案版本。\n104. 第二工作小組於其第六次會議審議由主席提交的決議草案。\n105. 下列締約方代表發表了聲明：貝南、巴西、象牙海岸、埃及、歐盟及其成員國、斐濟（代表太平洋小島嶼開發中國家）、印度、日本、馬拉威、摩洛哥、紐西蘭、奈及利亞、挪威、巴拿馬、巴拉圭、菲律賓、塞內加爾、巴勒斯坦國及英國。\n106. 第二工作小組同意在非正式討論後，於稍後的會議中恢復對該決議草案的審議。","html":"<p>議程項目 8<br />\n卡塔赫納生物安全議定書有效性之評估與審查，以及議定書執行計畫與能力建構行動計畫之中期評估<br />\n101. 第二工作小組於其第一次會議開始審議議程項目 8。其面前有一份決議草案。<sup>29</sup> 此外，秘書處關於卡塔赫納生物安全議定書有效性第五次評估與審查，以及議定書執行計畫與能力建構行動計畫之中期評估之資訊分析說明<sup>30</sup>，亦已作為參考文件提供。<br />\n102. 巴拿馬代表發表了聲明。<br />\n103. 主席表示，他將視需要進行非正式諮商，並諮詢秘書處以準備一份修訂後的決議草案版本。<br />\n104. 第二工作小組於其第六次會議審議由主席提交的決議草案。<br />\n105. 下列締約方代表發表了聲明：貝南、巴西、象牙海岸、埃及、歐盟及其成員國、斐濟（代表太平洋小島嶼開發中國家）、印度、日本、馬拉威、摩洛哥、紐西蘭、奈及利亞、挪威、巴拿馬、巴拉圭、菲律賓、塞內加爾、巴勒斯坦國及英國。<br />\n106. 第二工作小組同意在非正式討論後，於稍後的會議中恢復對該決議草案的審議。</p>","en":[13,14,15,16,17]},{"md":"$^{27}$ CBD/CP/MOP/12/2, 項目 7。\n$^{28}$ CBD/CP/MOP/12/6。\n$^{29}$ CBD/CP/MOP/12/2, 項目 8。\n$^{30}$ CBD/SBI/7/6/Add.1。","html":"<p><sup>27</sup> CBD/CP/MOP/12/2, 項目 7。<br />\n<sup>28</sup> CBD/CP/MOP/12/6。<br />\n<sup>29</sup> CBD/CP/MOP/12/2, 項目 8。<br />\n<sup>30</sup> CBD/SBI/7/6/Add.1。</p>","en":[18,19,20,21,22]}]},{"p":"p010","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ae39ed27b12c517cf05e7cd/p010.md","en":[{"t":"CBD/COP/17/WG.II/L.1-CBD/CP/MOP/12/WG.II/L.1"},{"t":"107.   At its 10th session, Working Group II resumed its consideration of the draft decision."},{"t":"108. Working Group II heard a report from the representative of Armenia on the outcome of the informal consultations."},{"t":"109. Working Group II approved the draft decision, as orally amended, for transmission to the plenary session as draft decision CBD/CP/MOP/12/L.10."},{"t":"Item 9"},{"t":"Matters related to the financial mechanism and resources"},{"t":"110. Working Group II began its consideration of agenda item 9 at its 2nd session. It had before it a draft decision,31 as well as a note by the Secretariat on matters related to the financial mechanism and resources.32"},{"t":"111. A representative of the Global Environment Facility presented the information set out in section II of the note by the Secretariat."},{"t":"112. As the modalities for the early submission of statements had been implemented for agenda item 9, with statements submitted pursuant to notification No. 2026-072, the Chair asked the Parties listed in annex III to document CBD/CP/MOP/12/INF/8 and present at the session whether they objected to their statements being considered as statements officially submitted for the present item. No objections were raised."},{"t":"113. Working Group II therefore agreed that the statements of the following Parties be considered as statements officially submitted under agenda item 9: Brazil, Chad, Côte d’Ivoire, European Union and its member States, Guatemala, Japan, Jordan and Norway."},{"t":"114. In addition, statements were made in session by representatives of the following Parties: Bahrain, Guatemala, Panama, Saudi Arabia, South Africa, Switzerland, United Republic of Tanzania and Zimbabwe (on behalf of the African States)."},{"t":"115. Following the exchange of views, the Chair said that he would prepare a revised version of the draft decision in consultation with the Secretariat, taking into account the views expressed by Parties."},{"t":"116. At its 5th session, Working Group II considered a draft decision submitted by the Chair."},{"t":"117. Statements were made by representatives of the following Parties: Brazil, Burkina Faso, China, Côte d’Ivoire, European Union and its member States, Japan, Kenya, Malawi, Niger, Norway, Panama, South Africa, Switzerland, United Kingdom, United Republic of Tanzania, Zambia and Zimbabwe (on behalf of the African States)."},{"t":"118. A statement was also made by a representative of the following non-Party: Equatorial Guinea."},{"t":"119. Working Group II agreed that interested Parties would hold informal discussions in order to find a solution for the remaining bracketed text."},{"t":"120. At its 6th session, Working Group II resumed its consideration of the draft decision."},{"t":"121. Statements were made by representatives of the following Parties: Armenia, European Union and its member States and Niger."},{"t":"122. Working Group II agreed to resume its consideration of the draft decision at a later session following further informal discussions."},{"t":"123. At its 7th session, Working Group II resumed its consideration of the draft decision."},{"t":"124. A representative of Armenia reported on the outcome of the informal discussions."},{"t":"31 CBD/CP/MOP/12/2, item 9."},{"t":"32 CBD/CP/MOP/12/7."},{"t":"10/15"}],"blocks":[{"md":"CBD/COP/17/WG.II/L.1-CBD/CP/MOP/12/WG.II/L.1","html":"<p>CBD/COP/17/WG.II/L.1-CBD/CP/MOP/12/WG.II/L.1</p>","en":[0,1,2]},{"md":"107.\n第二工作小組於其第十次會議中，恢復對決議草案之審議。","html":"<p>107.<br />\n第二工作小組於其第十次會議中，恢復對決議草案之審議。</p>","en":[3,4,5,6,7]},{"md":"108. 第二工作小組聽取了亞美尼亞代表關於非正式諮商結果之報告。\n109. 第二工作小組通過了經口頭修正之決議草案，並將其作為決議草案 CBD/CP/MOP/12/L.10 送交全會。","html":"<p>108. 第二工作小組聽取了亞美尼亞代表關於非正式諮商結果之報告。<br />\n109. 第二工作小組通過了經口頭修正之決議草案，並將其作為決議草案 CBD/CP/MOP/12/L.10 送交全會。</p>","en":[8,9,10,11,12]},{"md":"議程第 9 項\n與財務機制及資源相關事項\n110. 第二工作小組於其第二次會議中開始審議議程第 9 項。其面前有一份決議草案,$^{31}$ 以及秘書處關於與財務機制及資源相關事項之說明書.$^{32}$\n111. 全球環境基金代表提報了秘書處說明書第二節所載之資訊。\n112. 由於議程第 9 項已實施提早提交聲明之程序，且聲明係根據第 2026-072 號通知提交，因此主席要求附件 III 記載於 CBD/CP/MOP/12/INF/8 之締約方，於會議中說明其是否反對將其聲明視為針對本議程正式提交之聲明。未有人提出異議。\n113. 因此，第二工作小組同意將下列締約方之聲明視為依議程第 9 項正式提交之聲明：巴西、查德、象牙海岸、歐盟及其成員國、瓜地馬拉、日本、約旦及挪威。\n114. 此外，下列締約方代表於會議中亦發表了聲明：巴林、瓜地馬拉、巴拿馬、沙烏地阿拉伯、南非、瑞士、坦尚尼亞聯合共和國及辛巴威（代表非洲國家）。\n115. 在意見交換後，主席表示將與秘書處諮商，並考量締約方所表達之意見，準備決議草案之修訂版本。\n116. 第二工作小組於其第五次會議中，審議了由主席提交之決議草案。\n117. 下列締約方代表發表了聲明：巴西、布吉納法索、中國、象牙海岸、歐盟及其成員國、日本、肯亞、馬拉威、尼日、挪威、巴拿馬、南非、瑞士、英國、坦尚尼亞聯合共和國、尚比亞及辛巴威（代表非洲國家）。\n118. 下列非締約方代表亦發表了聲明：赤道幾內亞。\n119. 第二工作小組同意，感興趣之締約方將進行非正式討論，以尋求剩餘方括號文字之解決方案。\n120. 第二工作小組於其第六次會議中，恢復對決議草案之審議。\n121. 下列締約方代表發表了聲明：亞美尼亞、歐盟及其成員國及尼日。\n122. 第二工作小組同意在進一步非正式討論後，於稍後之會議中恢復對決議草案之審議。\n123. 第二工作小組於其第七次會議中，恢復對決議草案之審議。\n124. 亞美尼亞代表報告了非正式討論之結果。","html":"<p>議程第 9 項<br />\n與財務機制及資源相關事項<br />\n110. 第二工作小組於其第二次會議中開始審議議程第 9 項。其面前有一份決議草案,<sup>31</sup> 以及秘書處關於與財務機制及資源相關事項之說明書.<sup>32</sup><br />\n111. 全球環境基金代表提報了秘書處說明書第二節所載之資訊。<br />\n112. 由於議程第 9 項已實施提早提交聲明之程序，且聲明係根據第 2026-072 號通知提交，因此主席要求附件 III 記載於 CBD/CP/MOP/12/INF/8 之締約方，於會議中說明其是否反對將其聲明視為針對本議程正式提交之聲明。未有人提出異議。<br />\n113. 因此，第二工作小組同意將下列締約方之聲明視為依議程第 9 項正式提交之聲明：巴西、查德、象牙海岸、歐盟及其成員國、瓜地馬拉、日本、約旦及挪威。<br />\n114. 此外，下列締約方代表於會議中亦發表了聲明：巴林、瓜地馬拉、巴拿馬、沙烏地阿拉伯、南非、瑞士、坦尚尼亞聯合共和國及辛巴威（代表非洲國家）。<br />\n115. 在意見交換後，主席表示將與秘書處諮商，並考量締約方所表達之意見，準備決議草案之修訂版本。<br />\n116. 第二工作小組於其第五次會議中，審議了由主席提交之決議草案。<br />\n117. 下列締約方代表發表了聲明：巴西、布吉納法索、中國、象牙海岸、歐盟及其成員國、日本、肯亞、馬拉威、尼日、挪威、巴拿馬、南非、瑞士、英國、坦尚尼亞聯合共和國、尚比亞及辛巴威（代表非洲國家）。<br />\n118. 下列非締約方代表亦發表了聲明：赤道幾內亞。<br />\n119. 第二工作小組同意，感興趣之締約方將進行非正式討論，以尋求剩餘方括號文字之解決方案。<br />\n120. 第二工作小組於其第六次會議中，恢復對決議草案之審議。<br />\n121. 下列締約方代表發表了聲明：亞美尼亞、歐盟及其成員國及尼日。<br />\n122. 第二工作小組同意在進一步非正式討論後，於稍後之會議中恢復對決議草案之審議。<br />\n123. 第二工作小組於其第七次會議中，恢復對決議草案之審議。<br />\n124. 亞美尼亞代表報告了非正式討論之結果。</p>","en":[13,14,15,16,17]},{"md":"$^{31}$ CBD/CP/MOP/12/2, 議程第 9 項。\n$^{32}$ CBD/CP/MOP/12/7。","html":"<p><sup>31</sup> CBD/CP/MOP/12/2, 議程第 9 項。<br />\n<sup>32</sup> CBD/CP/MOP/12/7。</p>","en":[18,19,20,21,22]}]},{"p":"p011","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ae39ed27b12c517cf05e7cd/p011.md","en":[{"t":"CBD/COP/17/WG.II/L.1-CBD/CP/MOP/12/WG.II/L.1"},{"t":"125. Statements were made by representatives of the following Parties: Fiji (on behalf of the Pacific small island developing States) and Panama."},{"t":"126. Working Group II approved the draft decision, as orally amended, for transmission to the plenary session as draft decision CBD/CP/MOP/12/L.9."},{"t":"Item 10"},{"t":"Operation and activities of the Biosafety Clearing-House"},{"t":"127. Working Group II began its consideration of agenda item 10 at its 2nd session. It had before it a draft decision,33 as well as a note by the Secretariat on the operation and activities of the Biosafety Clearing-House.34"},{"t":"128. As the modalities for the early submission of statements had been implemented for agenda item 10, with statements submitted pursuant to notification No. 2026-072, the Chair asked the Parties listed in annex IV to document CBD/CP/MOP/12/INF/8 and present at the session whether they objected to their statements being considered as statements officially submitted for the present item. No objections were raised."},{"t":"129. Working Group II therefore agreed that the statements of the following Parties be considered as statements officially submitted under agenda item 10: Chad, Colombia, Eswatini, European Union and its member States, Guatemala, Japan, Norway, Senegal and Switzerland."},{"t":"130. In addition, statements were made in session by representatives of the following Parties: Bahrain, Egypt (on behalf of the African States), India, Nigeria, Peru, Saudi Arabia, Sudan, Tunisia, Zambia and Zimbabwe."},{"t":"131. Following the exchange of views, the Chair said that he would prepare a revised version of the draft decision in consultation with the Secretariat, taking into account the views expressed by Parties."},{"t":"132. At its 5th session, Working Group II considered a draft decision submitted by the Chair."},{"t":"133. Statements were made by representatives of the following Parties: European Union and its member States, Guatemala, Japan, New Zealand, Norway, Panama and Peru."},{"t":"134. Working Group II approved the draft decision, as orally amended, for transmission to the plenary session as draft decision CBD/CP/MOP/12/L.5."},{"t":"Item 11"},{"t":"Cooperation with international organizations,"},{"t":"bodies established under other conventions, and initiatives"},{"t":"135. Working Group II began its consideration of agenda item 11 at its 2nd session. It had before it a draft decision,35 as well as a note by the Secretariat on cooperation with international organizations, bodies established under other conventions, and initiatives.36"},{"t":"136. As the modalities for the early submission of statements had been implemented for agenda item 11, with statements submitted pursuant to notification No. 2026-072, the Chair asked the Parties listed in annex V to document CBD/CP/MOP/12/INF/8 and present at the session whether they objected to their statements being considered as statements officially submitted for the present item. No objections were raised."},{"t":"33 CBD/CP/MOP/12/2, item 10."},{"t":"34 CBD/CP/MOP/12/8."},{"t":"35 CBD/CP/MOP/12/2, item 11."},{"t":"36 CBD/CP/MOP/12/9."},{"t":"11/15"}],"blocks":[{"md":"CBD/COP/17/WG.II/L.1-CBD/CP/MOP/12/WG.II/L.1","html":"<p>CBD/COP/17/WG.II/L.1-CBD/CP/MOP/12/WG.II/L.1</p>","en":[0,1]},{"md":"125. 以下締約方代表發表了聲明：斐濟（代表太平洋小島嶼開發中國家）及巴拿馬。\n126. 第二工作小組通過了經口頭修正的決議草案，並將其作為決議草案 CBD/CP/MOP/12/L.9 送交全會。","html":"<p>125. 以下締約方代表發表了聲明：斐濟（代表太平洋小島嶼開發中國家）及巴拿馬。<br />\n126. 第二工作小組通過了經口頭修正的決議草案，並將其作為決議草案 CBD/CP/MOP/12/L.9 送交全會。</p>","en":[2,3,4,5,6]},{"md":"議程項目 10\n生物安全資訊交換所之運作與活動\n127. 第二工作小組於其第二次會議開始審議議程項目 10。其面前有一份決議草案,$^{33}$ 以及秘書處關於生物安全資訊交換所運作與活動的說明文件.$^{34}$\n128. 由於議程項目 10 已實施聲明提早提交之方式，且聲明係根據第 2026-072 號通知提交，主席詢問附件 IV 所列之文件 CBD/CP/MOP/12/INF/8 及其出席本次會議之締約方，是否反對其聲明被視為針對本項目正式提交之聲明。未提出異議。\n129. 因此，第二工作小組同意將以下締約方之聲明視為根據議程項目 10 正式提交之聲明：查德、哥倫比亞、史瓦帝尼、歐盟及其成員國、瓜地馬拉、日本、挪威、塞內加爾及瑞士。\n130. 此外，以下締約方代表於會議中發表了聲明：巴林、埃及（代表非洲國家）、印度、奈及利亞、秘魯、沙烏地阿拉伯、蘇丹、突尼西亞、尚比亞及辛巴威。\n131. 在交換意見後，主席表示將與秘書處協商，並考慮締約方所表達之意見，準備一份修訂後的決議草案。\n132. 第二工作小組於其第五次會議審議了由主席提交的一份決議草案。\n133. 以下締約方代表發表了聲明：歐盟及其成員國、瓜地馬拉、日本、紐西蘭、挪威、巴拿馬及秘魯。\n134. 第二工作小組通過了經口頭修正的決議草案，並將其作為決議草案 CBD/CP/MOP/12/L.5 送交全會。","html":"<p>議程項目 10<br />\n生物安全資訊交換所之運作與活動<br />\n127. 第二工作小組於其第二次會議開始審議議程項目 10。其面前有一份決議草案,<sup>33</sup> 以及秘書處關於生物安全資訊交換所運作與活動的說明文件.<sup>34</sup><br />\n128. 由於議程項目 10 已實施聲明提早提交之方式，且聲明係根據第 2026-072 號通知提交，主席詢問附件 IV 所列之文件 CBD/CP/MOP/12/INF/8 及其出席本次會議之締約方，是否反對其聲明被視為針對本項目正式提交之聲明。未提出異議。<br />\n129. 因此，第二工作小組同意將以下締約方之聲明視為根據議程項目 10 正式提交之聲明：查德、哥倫比亞、史瓦帝尼、歐盟及其成員國、瓜地馬拉、日本、挪威、塞內加爾及瑞士。<br />\n130. 此外，以下締約方代表於會議中發表了聲明：巴林、埃及（代表非洲國家）、印度、奈及利亞、秘魯、沙烏地阿拉伯、蘇丹、突尼西亞、尚比亞及辛巴威。<br />\n131. 在交換意見後，主席表示將與秘書處協商，並考慮締約方所表達之意見，準備一份修訂後的決議草案。<br />\n132. 第二工作小組於其第五次會議審議了由主席提交的一份決議草案。<br />\n133. 以下締約方代表發表了聲明：歐盟及其成員國、瓜地馬拉、日本、紐西蘭、挪威、巴拿馬及秘魯。<br />\n134. 第二工作小組通過了經口頭修正的決議草案，並將其作為決議草案 CBD/CP/MOP/12/L.5 送交全會。</p>","en":[7,8,9,10,11]},{"md":"議程項目 11\n與國際組織、依其他公約成立之機構及倡議之合作\n135. 第二工作小組於其第二次會議開始審議議程項目 11。其面前有一份決議草案,$^{35}$ 以及秘書處關於與國際組織、依其他公約成立之機構及倡議之合作的說明文件.$^{36}$\n136. 由於議程項目 11 已實施聲明提早提交之方式，且聲明係根據第 2026-072 號通知提交，主席詢問附件 V 所列之文件 CBD/CP/MOP/12/INF/8 及其出席本次會議之締約方，是否反對其聲明被視為針對本項目正式提交之聲明。未提出異議。","html":"<p>議程項目 11<br />\n與國際組織、依其他公約成立之機構及倡議之合作<br />\n135. 第二工作小組於其第二次會議開始審議議程項目 11。其面前有一份決議草案,<sup>35</sup> 以及秘書處關於與國際組織、依其他公約成立之機構及倡議之合作的說明文件.<sup>36</sup><br />\n136. 由於議程項目 11 已實施聲明提早提交之方式，且聲明係根據第 2026-072 號通知提交，主席詢問附件 V 所列之文件 CBD/CP/MOP/12/INF/8 及其出席本次會議之締約方，是否反對其聲明被視為針對本項目正式提交之聲明。未提出異議。</p>","en":[12,13,14,15,16]},{"md":"$^{33}$ CBD/CP/MOP/12/2, 項目 10。\n$^{34}$ CBD/CP/MOP/12/8。\n$^{35}$ CBD/CP/MOP/12/2, 項目 11。\n$^{36}$ CBD/CP/MOP/12/9。","html":"<p><sup>33</sup> CBD/CP/MOP/12/2, 項目 10。<br />\n<sup>34</sup> CBD/CP/MOP/12/8。<br />\n<sup>35</sup> CBD/CP/MOP/12/2, 項目 11。<br />\n<sup>36</sup> CBD/CP/MOP/12/9。</p>","en":[17,18,19,20,21]},{"md":"11/15","html":"<p>11/15</p>","en":[22]}]},{"p":"p012","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ae39ed27b12c517cf05e7cd/p012.md","en":[{"t":"CBD/COP/17/WG.II/L.1-CBD/CP/MOP/12/WG.II/L.1"},{"t":"137. Working Group II therefore agreed that the statements of the following Parties be considered as statements officially submitted under agenda item 11: Chad, European Union and its member States, Norway and Switzerland."},{"t":"138. In addition, statements were made in session by representatives of the following Parties: Antigua and Barbuda, Bahrain, Brazil, Germany and Slovenia."},{"t":"139. Statements were also made in session by representatives of the Economic Commission for Europe and the International Centre for Genetic Engineering and Biotechnology."},{"t":"140. Working Group II took note of the information provided."},{"t":"Item 13"},{"t":"Risk assessment and risk management of living modified organisms"},{"t":"141. Working Group II began its consideration of agenda item 13 at its 1st session. It had before it a draft decision.37 An information document containing a synthesis of submissions on experiences and assessment of applicability of the additional voluntary guidance materials to support case-by-case risk assessment of living modified organisms containing engineered gene drives38 had also been issued in relation to item 13."},{"t":"142. Working Group II agreed to establish a contact group, co-chaired by Martha Kandawa-Schulz (Namibia) and Werner Schenkel (Germany), with the mandate to resolve the bracketed text in the draft decision, including in connection with additional voluntary guidance materials."},{"t":"143. At its 8th session, Working Group II heard a report by one of the Co-Chairs of the contact group on the outcome of the group’s work."},{"t":"144.   At its 10th session, Working Group II resumed its consideration of the draft decision."},{"t":"145. Statements were made by representatives of the following Parties: Belarus, Brazil, European Union and its member States, India, Kenya, Malawi, Mexico, New Zealand, Norway, Panama, South Africa, Uganda and Zambia."},{"t":"146. Working Group II approved the draft decision, as orally amended, for transmission to the plenary session as draft decision CBD/CP/MOP/12/L.11."},{"t":"Item 14"},{"t":"Detection and identification of living modified organisms"},{"t":"147. Working Group II began its consideration of agenda item 14 at its 2nd session. It had before it a draft decision, 39 as well as a note by the Secretariat on detection and identification of living modified organisms. 40 The following information documents had also been issued in relation to agenda item 14: a summary of the online discussions of the Network of Laboratories for the Detection and Identification of Living Modified Organisms41 and a synthesis of submissions of information on the detection and identification of living modified organisms.42"},{"t":"148. As the modalities for the early submission of statements had been implemented for agenda item 14, with statements submitted pursuant to notification No. 2026-072, the Chair asked the Parties and observer listed in annex VI to document CBD/CP/MOP/12/INF/8 and present at the session whether they objected to their statements being considered as statements officially submitted for the present item. No objections were raised."},{"t":"37 CBD/CP/MOP/12/2, item 13."},{"t":"38 CBD/CP/MOP/12/INF/3."},{"t":"39 CBD/CP/MOP/12/2, item 14."},{"t":"40 CBD/CP/MOP/12/10."},{"t":"41 CBD/CP/MOP/12/INF/4."},{"t":"42 CBD/CP/MOP/12/INF/5."},{"t":"12/15"}],"blocks":[{"md":"CBD/COP/17/WG.II/L.1-CBD/CP/MOP/12/WG.II/L.1","html":"<p>CBD/COP/17/WG.II/L.1-CBD/CP/MOP/12/WG.II/L.1</p>","en":[0,1]},{"md":"137. 因此，第二工作小組同意將下列締約方之聲明視為依議程項目 11 正式提交之聲明：查德、歐盟及其成員國、挪威與瑞士。\n13  8. 此外，下列締約方代表於會議期間亦發表了聲明：安地卡及巴布達、巴林、巴西、德國與斯洛維尼亞。\n139. 歐洲經濟委員會與國際遺傳工程與生物技術中心之代表亦於會議期間發表了聲明。\n140. 第二工作小組**注意到**所提供的資訊。","html":"<p>137. 因此，第二工作小組同意將下列締約方之聲明視為依議程項目 11 正式提交之聲明：查德、歐盟及其成員國、挪威與瑞士。<br />\n13  8. 此外，下列締約方代表於會議期間亦發表了聲明：安地卡及巴布達、巴林、巴西、德國與斯洛維尼亞。<br />\n139. 歐洲經濟委員會與國際遺傳工程與生物技術中心之代表亦於會議期間發表了聲明。<br />\n140. 第二工作小組<strong>注意到</strong>所提供的資訊。</p>","en":[2,3,4,5,6]},{"md":"議程項目 13\n基因改造活生物體之風險評估與風險管理\n141. 第二工作小組於其第一次會議開始審議議程項目 13。其面前有一份決議草案。³⁷ 關於「針對支持含有基因驅動工程之基因改造活生物體個案風險評估，其附加自願性指引材料之經驗與適用性評估提交內容之綜合報告」³⁸ 之資訊文件，亦已針對議程項目 13 發布。\n142. 第二工作小組同意成立一個聯絡小組，由 Martha Kandawa-Schulz（納米比亞）與 Werner Schenkel（德國）共同主持，其任務為解決決議草案中之方括號文字，包括與附加自願性指引材料相關之文字。\n143. 第二工作小組於其第八次會議聽取了聯絡小組其中一位共同主席關於該小組工作成果之報告。\n144. 第二工作小組於其第十次會議恢復審議該決議草案。\n145. 下列締約方代表發表了聲明：白俄羅斯、巴西、歐盟及其成員國、印度、肯亞、馬拉威、墨西哥、紐西蘭、挪威、巴拿馬、南非、烏干達與尚比亞。\n146. 第二工作小組通過了經口頭修正之決議草案，並將其作為決議草案 CBD/CP/MOP/12/L.11 提交至全體會議。","html":"<p>議程項目 13<br />\n基因改造活生物體之風險評估與風險管理<br />\n141. 第二工作小組於其第一次會議開始審議議程項目 13。其面前有一份決議草案。³⁷ 關於「針對支持含有基因驅動工程之基因改造活生物體個案風險評估，其附加自願性指引材料之經驗與適用性評估提交內容之綜合報告」³⁸ 之資訊文件，亦已針對議程項目 13 發布。<br />\n142. 第二工作小組同意成立一個聯絡小組，由 Martha Kandawa-Schulz（納米比亞）與 Werner Schenkel（德國）共同主持，其任務為解決決議草案中之方括號文字，包括與附加自願性指引材料相關之文字。<br />\n143. 第二工作小組於其第八次會議聽取了聯絡小組其中一位共同主席關於該小組工作成果之報告。<br />\n144. 第二工作小組於其第十次會議恢復審議該決議草案。<br />\n145. 下列締約方代表發表了聲明：白俄羅斯、巴西、歐盟及其成員國、印度、肯亞、馬拉威、墨西哥、紐西蘭、挪威、巴拿馬、南非、烏干達與尚比亞。<br />\n146. 第二工作小組通過了經口頭修正之決議草案，並將其作為決議草案 CBD/CP/MOP/12/L.11 提交至全體會議。</p>","en":[7,8,9,10,11]},{"md":"議程項目 14\n基因改造活生物體之偵測與鑑定\n147. 第二工作小組於其第二次會議開始審議議程項目 14。其面前有一份決議草案³⁹，以及秘書處關於基因改造活生物體偵測與鑑定之說明。⁴⁰ 關於議程項目 14，亦已發布下列資訊文件：「基因改造活生物體偵測與鑑定實驗室網絡」線上討論摘要⁴¹，以及關於基因改造活生物體偵測與鑑定之資訊提交內容綜合報告。⁴²\n148. 由於議程項目 14 已實施聲明早期提交之程序，且聲明係依據第 2026-072 號通知提交，主席請求附件 VI 所示之締約方與觀察員（文件編號 CBD/CP/MOP/12/INF/8）於會議期間說明，是否反對其聲明被視為針對本項目正式提交之聲明。無人提出異議。","html":"<p>議程項目 14<br />\n基因改造活生物體之偵測與鑑定<br />\n147. 第二工作小組於其第二次會議開始審議議程項目 14。其面前有一份決議草案³⁹，以及秘書處關於基因改造活生物體偵測與鑑定之說明。⁴⁰ 關於議程項目 14，亦已發布下列資訊文件：「基因改造活生物體偵測與鑑定實驗室網絡」線上討論摘要⁴¹，以及關於基因改造活生物體偵測與鑑定之資訊提交內容綜合報告。⁴²<br />\n148. 由於議程項目 14 已實施聲明早期提交之程序，且聲明係依據第 2026-072 號通知提交，主席請求附件 VI 所示之締約方與觀察員（文件編號 CBD/CP/MOP/12/INF/8）於會議期間說明，是否反對其聲明被視為針對本項目正式提交之聲明。無人提出異議。</p>","en":[12,13,14,15,16]},{"md":"³⁷ CBD/CP/MOP/12/2，項目 13。\n³⁸ CBD/CP/MOP/12/INF/3。\n³⁹ CBD/CP/MOP/12/2，項目 14。\n⁴⁰ CBD/CP/MOP/12/10。\n⁴¹ CBD/CP/MOP/12/INF/4。\n⁴² CBD/CP/MOP/12/INF/5。","html":"<p>³⁷ CBD/CP/MOP/12/2，項目 13。<br />\n³⁸ CBD/CP/MOP/12/INF/3。<br />\n³⁹ CBD/CP/MOP/12/2，項目 14。<br />\n⁴⁰ CBD/CP/MOP/12/10。<br />\n⁴¹ CBD/CP/MOP/12/INF/4。<br />\n⁴² CBD/CP/MOP/12/INF/5。</p>","en":[17,18,19,20,21]}]},{"p":"p013","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ae39ed27b12c517cf05e7cd/p013.md","en":[{"t":"CBD/COP/17/WG.II/L.1-CBD/CP/MOP/12/WG.II/L.1"},{"t":"149. Working Group II therefore agreed that the statements of the following Parties be considered as statements officially submitted under agenda item 14: Brazil, Chad, Dominican Republic, European Union and its member States, Guatemala, Japan, Norway, Republic of Korea, Senegal and Switzerland."},{"t":"150. Working Group II also agreed that the statement of the CBD Alliance be considered as a statement officially submitted under agenda item 14."},{"t":"151. In addition, statements were made in session by representatives of the following Parties: Burkina Faso, Costa Rica, Côte d’Ivoire, Egypt, Ghana, India, Indonesia, Kenya (on behalf of the African States), Mexico, Nigeria, Panama (also on behalf of Paraguay), Peru, Rwanda, Sudan, Thailand, Tunisia, Uganda and Zambia."},{"t":"152. Following the exchange of views, the Chair said that he would prepare a revised version of the draft decision in consultation with the Secretariat, taking into account the views expressed or supported by Parties."},{"t":"153. At its 5th session, Working Group II considered a draft decision submitted by the Chair."},{"t":"154. Statements were made by representatives of the following Parties: Brazil, Democratic Republic of the Congo, European Union and its member States, Guatemala, Kenya, Nigeria, Panama, Paraguay and Uganda."},{"t":"155. Working Group II approved the draft decision, as orally amended, for transmission to the plenary session as draft decision CBD/CP/MOP/12/L.7."},{"t":"Item 15"},{"t":"Socioeconomic considerations"},{"t":"156. Working Group II began its consideration of agenda item 15 at its 2nd session. It had before it a draft decision,43 as well as a note by the Secretariat on socioeconomic considerations.44"},{"t":"157. As the modalities for the early submission of statements had been implemented for agenda item 15, with statements submitted pursuant to notification No. 2026-072, the Chair asked the Parties and observer listed in annex VII to document CBD/CP/MOP/12/INF/8 and present at the session whether they objected to their statements being considered as statements officially submitted for the present item. No objections were raised."},{"t":"158. Working Group II therefore agreed that the statements of the following Parties be considered as statements officially submitted under agenda item 15: Chad, European Union and its member States, Japan, Norway and Switzerland."},{"t":"159. Working Group II also agreed that the statement of the CBD Alliance be considered as a statement officially submitted under agenda item 15."},{"t":"160. In addition, statements were made in session by representatives of the following Parties: Côte d’Ivoire, Panama (also on behalf of Paraguay), Peru, Nigeria, Zambia and Zimbabwe (on behalf of the African States)."},{"t":"161. Following the exchange of views, the Chair said that he would prepare a revised version of the draft decision in consultation with the Secretariat, taking into account the views expressed or supported by Parties."},{"t":"162. At its 5th session, Working Group II considered a draft decision submitted by the Chair."},{"t":"163. Statements were made by representatives of the following Parties: Brazil, Malawi, Norway, Panama, Peru, United Republic of Tanzania and Uruguay."},{"t":"43 CBD/CP/MOP/12/2, item 15."},{"t":"44 CBD/CP/MOP/12/11."},{"t":"13/15"}],"blocks":[{"md":"CBD/COP/17/WG.II/L.1-CBD/CP/MOP/12/WG.II/L.1","html":"<p>CBD/COP/17/WG.II/L.1-CBD/CP/MOP/12/WG.II/L.1</p>","en":[0,1,2]},{"md":"149. 因此，第二工作小組同意將下列締約方之聲明視為依議程項目 14 正式提交之聲明：巴西、查德、多明尼加共和國、歐盟及其成員國、瓜地馬拉、日本、挪威、大韓民國、塞內加爾及瑞士。\n150. 第二工作小組亦同意將 CBD Alliance 之聲明視為依議程項目 14 正式提交之聲明。\n151. 此外，下列締約方代表於會議中亦發表了聲明：布吉納法索、哥斯大黎加、象牙海岸、埃及、迦納、印度、印尼、肯亞（代表非洲國家）、墨西哥、奈及利亞、巴拿馬（亦代表巴拉圭）、秘魯、盧安達、蘇丹、泰國、突尼西亞、烏干達及尚比亞。\n152. 意見交流後，主席表示將與秘書處協商，並考量締約方所表達或支持之意見，準備決議草案之修訂版本。\n153. 第二工作小組於其第五次會議審議了由主席提交之決議草案。\n154. 下列締約方代表發表了聲明：巴西、剛果民主共和國、歐盟及其成員國、瓜地馬拉、肯亞、奈及利亞、巴拿馬、巴拉圭及烏干達。\n155. 第二工作小組通過經口頭修正之決議草案，並將其作為決議草案 CBD/CP/MOP/12/L.7 提交全會。","html":"<p>149. 因此，第二工作小組同意將下列締約方之聲明視為依議程項目 14 正式提交之聲明：巴西、查德、多明尼加共和國、歐盟及其成員國、瓜地馬拉、日本、挪威、大韓民國、塞內加爾及瑞士。<br />\n150. 第二工作小組亦同意將 CBD Alliance 之聲明視為依議程項目 14 正式提交之聲明。<br />\n151. 此外，下列締約方代表於會議中亦發表了聲明：布吉納法索、哥斯大黎加、象牙海岸、埃及、迦納、印度、印尼、肯亞（代表非洲國家）、墨西哥、奈及利亞、巴拿馬（亦代表巴拉圭）、秘魯、盧安達、蘇丹、泰國、突尼西亞、烏干達及尚比亞。<br />\n152. 意見交流後，主席表示將與秘書處協商，並考量締約方所表達或支持之意見，準備決議草案之修訂版本。<br />\n153. 第二工作小組於其第五次會議審議了由主席提交之決議草案。<br />\n154. 下列締約方代表發表了聲明：巴西、剛果民主共和國、歐盟及其成員國、瓜地馬拉、肯亞、奈及利亞、巴拿馬、巴拉圭及烏干達。<br />\n155. 第二工作小組通過經口頭修正之決議草案，並將其作為決議草案 CBD/CP/MOP/12/L.7 提交全會。</p>","en":[3,4,5,6,7]},{"md":"議程項目 15\n社會經濟考量\n156. 第二工作小組於其第二次會議開始審議議程項目 15。其面前有一份決議草案，$^{43}$ 以及秘書處關於社會經濟考量之說明文件。$^{44}$\n157. 由於議程項目 15 已實施聲明早期提交之程序，且聲明係依通知編號 2026-072 提交，主席詢問附件 VII 所示之文件 CBD/CP/MOP/12/INF/8 所列締約方與觀察員，於會議中是否反對其聲明被視為本項目正式提交之聲明。未提出任何反對意見。\n158. 因此，第二工作小組同意將下列締約方之聲明視為依議程項目 15 正式提交之聲明：查德、歐盟及其成員國、日本、挪威及瑞士。\n159. 第二工作小組亦同意將 CBD Alliance 之聲明視為依議程項目 15 正式提交之聲明。\n160. 此外，下列締約方代表於會議中亦發表了聲明：象牙海岸、巴拿馬（亦代表巴拉圭）、秘魯、奈及利亞、尚比亞及辛巴威（代表非洲國家）。\n161. 意見交流後，主席表示將與秘書處協商，並考量締約方所表達或支持之意見，準備決議草案之修訂版本。\n162. 第二工作小組於其第五次會議審議了由主席提交之決議草案。\n163. 下列締約方代表發表了聲明：巴西、馬拉威、挪威、巴拿馬、秘魯、坦尚尼亞聯合共和國及烏拉圭。","html":"<p>議程項目 15<br />\n社會經濟考量<br />\n156. 第二工作小組於其第二次會議開始審議議程項目 15。其面前有一份決議草案，<sup>43</sup> 以及秘書處關於社會經濟考量之說明文件。<sup>44</sup><br />\n157. 由於議程項目 15 已實施聲明早期提交之程序，且聲明係依通知編號 2026-072 提交，主席詢問附件 VII 所示之文件 CBD/CP/MOP/12/INF/8 所列締約方與觀察員，於會議中是否反對其聲明被視為本項目正式提交之聲明。未提出任何反對意見。<br />\n158. 因此，第二工作小組同意將下列締約方之聲明視為依議程項目 15 正式提交之聲明：查德、歐盟及其成員國、日本、挪威及瑞士。<br />\n159. 第二工作小組亦同意將 CBD Alliance 之聲明視為依議程項目 15 正式提交之聲明。<br />\n160. 此外，下列締約方代表於會議中亦發表了聲明：象牙海岸、巴拿馬（亦代表巴拉圭）、秘魯、奈及利亞、尚比亞及辛巴威（代表非洲國家）。<br />\n161. 意見交流後，主席表示將與秘書處協商，並考量締約方所表達或支持之意見，準備決議草案之修訂版本。<br />\n162. 第二工作小組於其第五次會議審議了由主席提交之決議草案。<br />\n163. 下列締約方代表發表了聲明：巴西、馬拉威、挪威、巴拿馬、秘魯、坦尚尼亞聯合共和國及烏拉圭。</p>","en":[10,11,12,13,14]},{"md":"$^{43}$ CBD/CP/MOP/12/2，項目 15。\n$^{44}$ CBD/CP/MOP/12/11。","html":"<p><sup>43</sup> CBD/CP/MOP/12/2，項目 15。<br />\n<sup>44</sup> CBD/CP/MOP/12/11。</p>","en":[15,16,17,18,19]}]},{"p":"p014","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ae39ed27b12c517cf05e7cd/p014.md","en":[{"t":"CBD/COP/17/WG.II/L.1-CBD/CP/MOP/12/WG.II/L.1"},{"t":"164. Working Group II approved the draft decision, as orally amended, for transmission to the plenary session as draft decision CBD/CP/MOP/12/L.4."},{"t":"Item 16"},{"t":"National legislation, regulations and guidelines"},{"t":"on new developments in modern biotechnology"},{"t":"165. Working Group II began its consideration of agenda item 16 at its 2nd session. It had before it a draft decision,45 as well as a note by the Secretariat containing information on national legislation, regulations and guidelines on new developments in modern biotechnology. 46 An information document containing additional information on national legislation, regulations and guidelines on new developments in modern biotechnology had also been issued in relation to agenda item 16.47"},{"t":"166. As the modalities for the early submission of statements had been implemented for agenda item 16, with statements submitted pursuant to notification No. 2026-072, the Chair asked the Parties and observer listed in annex VIII to document CBD/CP/MOP/12/INF/8 and present at the session whether they objected to their statements being considered as statements officially submitted for the present item. No objections were raised."},{"t":"167. Working Group II therefore agreed that the statements of the following Parties be considered as statements officially submitted under agenda item 16: Brazil, Chad, Colombia, European Union and its member States, Japan, Norway, Republic of Korea and Switzerland."},{"t":"168. Working Group II also agreed that the statement of the CBD Alliance be considered as a statement officially submitted under agenda item 16."},{"t":"169. In addition, statements were made in session by representatives of the following Parties: Bahrain, Burkina Faso (on behalf of the African States), Costa Rica, Côte d’Ivoire, Democratic Republic of the Congo, Indonesia, Nigeria, Panama, Paraguay, Saudi Arabia, Senegal, Thailand and Uganda."},{"t":"170. Following the exchange of views, the Chair said that he would prepare a revised version of the draft decision in consultation with the Secretariat, taking into account the views expressed or supported by Parties."},{"t":"171. At its 6th session, Working Group II considered a draft decision submitted by the Chair."},{"t":"172. Statements were made by representatives of the following Parties: Brazil, Burkina Faso, Cameroon, European Union and its member States, Guatemala, New Zealand, Nigeria, Norway, Panama, Paraguay and Peru."},{"t":"173. Working Group II approved the draft decision, as orally amended, for transmission to the plenary session as draft decision CBD/CP/MOP/12/L.8."},{"t":"Item 17"},{"t":"Nagoya-Kuala Lumpur Supplementary Protocol on Liability and Redress"},{"t":"174. Working Group II began its consideration of agenda item 17 at its 3rd session. It had before it a draft decision,48 as well as a note by the Secretariat on the Nagoya-Kuala Lumpur Supplementary Protocol on Liability and Redress.49"},{"t":"175. As the modalities for the early submission of statements had been implemented for agenda item 17, with statements submitted pursuant to notification No. 2026-072, the Chair asked the Parties"},{"t":"45 CBD/CP/MOP/12/2, item 16."},{"t":"46 CBD/CP/MOP/12/12."},{"t":"47 CBD/CP/MOP/12/INF/6."},{"t":"48 CBD/CP/MOP/12/2, item 17."},{"t":"49 CBD/CP/MOP/12/13."},{"t":"14/15"}],"blocks":[{"md":"CBD/COP/17/WG.II/L.1-CBD/CP/MOP/12/WG.II/L.1","html":"<p>CBD/COP/17/WG.II/L.1-CBD/CP/MOP/12/WG.II/L.1</p>","en":[0]},{"md":"164. 第二工作小組通過了經口頭修正之決議草案，並擬將其作為決議草案 CBD/CP/MOP/12/L.4 提交全會。","html":"<p>164. 第二工作小組通過了經口頭修正之決議草案，並擬將其作為決議草案 CBD/CP/MOP/12/L.4 提交全會。</p>","en":[1]},{"md":"議程項目 16\n現代生物技術新發展之國家立法、法規與指南\n165. 第二工作小組於其第二次會議開始審議議程項目 16。其面前有一份決議草案,$^{45}$ 以及秘書處關於現代生物技術新發展之國家立法、法規與指南資訊之說明書.$^{46}$ 針對議程項目 16，亦已發布一份包含現代生物技術新發展之國家立法、法規與指南額外資訊的資訊文件.$^{47}$","html":"<p>議程項目 16<br />\n現代生物技術新發展之國家立法、法規與指南<br />\n165. 第二工作小組於其第二次會議開始審議議程項目 16。其面前有一份決議草案,<sup>45</sup> 以及秘書處關於現代生物技術新發展之國家立法、法規與指南資訊之說明書.<sup>46</sup> 針對議程項目 16，亦已發布一份包含現代生物技術新發展之國家立法、法規與指南額外資訊的資訊文件.<sup>47</sup></p>","en":[2,3,4,5]},{"md":"166. 由於議程項目 16 已實施提前提交聲明的程序，且聲明係根據通知編號 2026-072 提交，因此主席詢問附件 VIII 所列之締約方與觀察員（見 CBD/CP/MOP/12/INF/8），是否反對其聲明被視為針對本項目正式提交之聲明。無人提出異議。","html":"<p>166. 由於議程項目 16 已實施提前提交聲明的程序，且聲明係根據通知編號 2026-072 提交，因此主席詢問附件 VIII 所列之締約方與觀察員（見 CBD/CP/MOP/12/INF/8），是否反對其聲明被視為針對本項目正式提交之聲明。無人提出異議。</p>","en":[6]},{"md":"167. 因此，第二工作小組同意將下列締約方之聲明視為於議程項目 16 下正式提交之聲明：巴西、查德、哥倫比亞、歐盟及其成員國、日本、挪威、大韓民國與瑞士。","html":"<p>167. 因此，第二工作小組同意將下列締約方之聲明視為於議程項目 16 下正式提交之聲明：巴西、查德、哥倫比亞、歐盟及其成員國、日本、挪威、大韓民國與瑞士。</p>","en":[7]},{"md":"168. 第二工作小組亦同意將 CBD 聯盟之聲明視為於議程項目 16 下正式提交之聲明。","html":"<p>168. 第二工作小組亦同意將 CBD 聯盟之聲明視為於議程項目 16 下正式提交之聲明。</p>","en":[8]},{"md":"169. 此外，下列締約方代表於會議中發表了聲明：巴林、布吉納法索（代表非洲國家）、哥斯大黎加、象牙海岸、剛果民主共和國、印尼、奈及利亞、巴拿馬、巴拉圭、沙烏地阿拉伯、塞內加爾、泰國與烏干達。","html":"<p>169. 此外，下列締約方代表於會議中發表了聲明：巴林、布吉納法索（代表非洲國家）、哥斯大黎加、象牙海岸、剛果民主共和國、印尼、奈及利亞、巴拿馬、巴拉圭、沙烏地阿拉伯、塞內加爾、泰國與烏干達。</p>","en":[9]},{"md":"170. 在意見交換後，主席表示將與秘書處協商，並考量締約方所表達或支持之意見，準備決議草案之修訂版本。","html":"<p>170. 在意見交換後，主席表示將與秘書處協商，並考量締約方所表達或支持之意見，準備決議草案之修訂版本。</p>","en":[10]},{"md":"171. 第二工作小組於其第六次會議審議了由主席提交之決議草案。","html":"<p>171. 第二工作小組於其第六次會議審議了由主席提交之決議草案。</p>","en":[11]},{"md":"172. 下列締約方代表發表了聲明：巴西、布吉納法索、喀麥隆、歐盟及其成員國、瓜地馬拉、紐西蘭、奈及利亞、挪威、巴拿馬、巴拉圭與秘魯。","html":"<p>172. 下列締約方代表發表了聲明：巴西、布吉納法索、喀麥隆、歐盟及其成員國、瓜地馬拉、紐西蘭、奈及利亞、挪威、巴拿馬、巴拉圭與秘魯。</p>","en":[12]},{"md":"173. 第二工作小組通過了經口頭修正之決議草案，並擬將其作為決議草案 CBD/CP/MOP/12/L.8 提交全會。","html":"<p>173. 第二工作小組通過了經口頭修正之決議草案，並擬將其作為決議草案 CBD/CP/MOP/12/L.8 提交全會。</p>","en":[13]},{"md":"議程項目 17\n名古屋－吉隆坡賠償責任與補救補充議定書\n174. 第二工作小組於其第三次會議開始審議議程項目 17。其面前有一份決議草案,$^{48}$ 以及秘書處關於名古屋－吉隆坡賠償責任與補救補充議定書之說明書.$^{49}$","html":"<p>議程項目 17<br />\n名古屋－吉隆坡賠償責任與補救補充議定書<br />\n174. 第二工作小組於其第三次會議開始審議議程項目 17。其面前有一份決議草案,<sup>48</sup> 以及秘書處關於名古屋－吉隆坡賠償責任與補救補充議定書之說明書.<sup>49</sup></p>","en":[14,15,16]},{"md":"175. 由於議程項目 17 已實施提前提交聲明的程序，且聲明係根據通知編號 2026-072 提交，主席詢問締約方","html":"<p>175. 由於議程項目 17 已實施提前提交聲明的程序，且聲明係根據通知編號 2026-072 提交，主席詢問締約方</p>","en":[17]},{"md":"---\n$^{45}$ CBD/CP/MOP/12/2, 項目 16。\n$^{46}$ CBD/CP/MOP/12/12。\n$^{47}$ CBD/CP/MOP/12/INF/6。\n$^{48}$ CBD/CP/MOP/12/2, 項目 17。\n$^{49}$ CBD/CP/MOP/12/13。","html":"<hr />\n<p><sup>45</sup> CBD/CP/MOP/12/2, 項目 16。<br />\n<sup>46</sup> CBD/CP/MOP/12/12。<br />\n<sup>47</sup> CBD/CP/MOP/12/INF/6。<br />\n<sup>48</sup> CBD/CP/MOP/12/2, 項目 17。<br />\n<sup>49</sup> CBD/CP/MOP/12/13。</p>","en":[18,19,20,21,22]}]},{"p":"p015","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ae39ed27b12c517cf05e7cd/p015.md","en":[{"t":"CBD/COP/17/WG.II/L.1-CBD/CP/MOP/12/WG.II/L.1"},{"t":"and observer listed in annex IX to document CBD/CP/MOP/12/INF/8 and present at the session whether they objected to their statements being considered as statements officially submitted for the present item. No objections were raised."},{"t":"176. Working Group II therefore agreed that the statements of the following Parties be considered as statements officially submitted under agenda item 17: European Union and its member States, Japan, Norway and Switzerland."},{"t":"177. Working Group II also agreed that the statement of Chad, a non-Party to the Supplementary Protocol, be considered as a statement officially submitted under agenda item 17."},{"t":"178. Working Group II further agreed that the statement of the CBD Alliance be considered as a statement officially submitted under agenda item 17."},{"t":"179. In addition, statements were made in session by representatives of the following Parties: Eswatini, Malawi (on behalf of the African States), Nigeria and Uganda."},{"t":"180. Following the exchange of views, the Chair said that he would prepare a revised version of the draft decision in consultation with the Secretariat, taking into account the views expressed or supported by Parties."},{"t":"181. At its 5th session, Working Group II considered a draft decision submitted by the Chair."},{"t":"182. Statements were made by representatives of the following Parties: European Union and its member States, Japan and Malawi."},{"t":"183. Working Group II approved the draft decision, as orally amended, for transmission to the plenary session as draft decision CBD/CP/MOP/12/L.3."},{"t":"__________"},{"t":"15/15"}],"blocks":[{"md":"CBD/COP/17/WG.II/L.1-CBD/CP/MOP/12/WG.II/L.1","html":"<p>CBD/COP/17/WG.II/L.1-CBD/CP/MOP/12/WG.II/L.1</p>","en":[0]},{"md":"以及列於文件 CBD/CP/MOP/12/INF/8 附件 IX 之觀察員，且出席本次會議者，是否反對其聲明被視為就本議案正式提交之聲明。無人提出異議。","html":"<p>以及列於文件 CBD/CP/MOP/12/INF/8 附件 IX 之觀察員，且出席本次會議者，是否反對其聲明被視為就本議案正式提交之聲明。無人提出異議。</p>","en":[1]},{"md":"176. 因此，第二工作小組同意將下列締約方之聲明視為依議程第 17 項正式提交之聲明：歐洲聯盟及其成員國、日本、挪威及瑞士。","html":"<p>176. 因此，第二工作小組同意將下列締約方之聲明視為依議程第 17 項正式提交之聲明：歐洲聯盟及其成員國、日本、挪威及瑞士。</p>","en":[2]},{"md":"177. 第二工作小組亦同意將非補充議定書締約方查德之聲明，視為依議程第 17 項正式提交之聲明。","html":"<p>177. 第二工作小組亦同意將非補充議定書締約方查德之聲明，視為依議程第 17 項正式提交之聲明。</p>","en":[3]},{"md":"178. 第二工作小組進一步同意將 CBD 聯盟之聲明，視為依議程第 17 項正式提交之聲明。","html":"<p>178. 第二工作小組進一步同意將 CBD 聯盟之聲明，視為依議程第 17 項正式提交之聲明。</p>","en":[4]},{"md":"179. 此外，下列締約方代表於會議中亦發表了聲明：史瓦帝尼、馬拉威（代表非洲國家）、奈及利亞及烏干達。","html":"<p>179. 此外，下列締約方代表於會議中亦發表了聲明：史瓦帝尼、馬拉威（代表非洲國家）、奈及利亞及烏干達。</p>","en":[5]},{"md":"180. 在意見交換後，主席表示將與秘書處協商，並考量締約方所表達或支持之意見，準備決議草案之修訂版本。","html":"<p>180. 在意見交換後，主席表示將與秘書處協商，並考量締約方所表達或支持之意見，準備決議草案之修訂版本。</p>","en":[6]},{"md":"181. 第二工作小組於第五次會議審議了由主席提交之決議草案。","html":"<p>181. 第二工作小組於第五次會議審議了由主席提交之決議草案。</p>","en":[7]},{"md":"182. 下列締約方代表發表了聲明：歐洲聯盟及其成員國、日本及馬拉威。","html":"<p>182. 下列締約方代表發表了聲明：歐洲聯盟及其成員國、日本及馬拉威。</p>","en":[8]},{"md":"183. 第二工作小組通過經口頭修正之決議草案，並將其作為決議草案 CBD/CP/MOP/12/L.3 提交全會。","html":"<p>183. 第二工作小組通過經口頭修正之決議草案，並將其作為決議草案 CBD/CP/MOP/12/L.3 提交全會。</p>","en":[9]},{"md":"__________","html":"<hr />","en":[9]},{"md":"15/15","html":"<p>15/15</p>","en":[10,11]}]}]};
